window.EB_SB_ADD({"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-11/adma-heavenstriker":{"lang":["Common","Shadowtongue","Vishkanyan"],"gear":["Rapier","Sample 73","Leather Armor","Giant Scorpion Venom (2)","Lethargy Poison (2)","Spider Venom (2)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Close Quarters","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Adma isn't Off-Guard to creatures of 8th-level or lower that are flanking her.</p>"},{"n":"Venom Spit","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Adma is targeted with a Strike by a creature within 30 feet</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Adma spits venom into the attacker's eyes. The attacker takes 2d6 poison damage (DC 23 basic Reflex save). On a failure, the creature is Off-Guard until the end of the target's next turn.</p>"},{"n":"Extend Potency","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> Adma has envenomed her weapon</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Adma spits on the blade, revitalizing the venom. The venom remains potent until the end of Adma's next turn.</p>"},{"n":"Quick Envenom","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Adma Interacts to draw her rapier, then applies a venom to it. The venom remains potent until the end of Adma's next turn, or until Adma hits a target or critically fails an attack roll.</p>"},{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Adma deals an extra 2d6 precision damage to Off-Guard creatures.</p>"},{"n":"Surprise Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>On the first round of combat, creatures that haven't acted yet are Off-Guard to Adma.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-13/animated-fang":{"description":"<p>The fang on the altar leaps up to stab at insufficiently zealous creatures.</p>","disable":"<p>The haunt is disabled once there aren't any creatures in the room that haven't sufficiently proclaimed their zeal (as described above).</p>","reset":"<p>If the fang is not destroyed, it returns to the altar and the haunt resets immediately.</p>","routine":"<p>(two-actions) The fang leaps around the room, flying up to 20 feet and making a fang Strike against a random creature in the room.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(expert) to notice the residual animating magic in the fang</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Leaping Fang","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature interacts with the items in this room without first proclaiming their zeal</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The haunt makes a fang Strike against the triggering creature, then rolls initiative.</p>"}],"strikeNotes":{"Fang":"<p>No multiple attack penalty</p>"}},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-08/ascending-the-chain":{"description":"<p>The PCs appear on a gigantic wall of hooked chains dangling in a gray swirling mist. The chains radiate life-chilling energy Cries of innocence and condemnation echo through the mist in Elven. A plane of light 10 feet above eddies and swirls as it dully reflects the PCs below, but the reflections warp and alter the PCs to have sallow complexions like the undead.</p>","disable":"<p>A PC that has ascended to the plane of light (DC 15 Athletics check to Climb; on a critical failure, the PC falls 10 feet before being seized by a chain) can attempt a DC 20 Thievery check to disrupt the plane or a DC 20 Arcana, DC 20 Occultism or DC 20 Religion check to ritually disrupt the haunting. Each success reduces the haunt's actions by one. When the haunt has no more actions, it is disabled and the PCs all return to area <strong>B3</strong>.</p>","reset":"<p>The haunt resets the next time the <em>Soulshackle</em> traps creatures in the library.</p>","routine":"<p>(three actions) The chains rattle and sigh ominously around two different random creatures trapped in the haunt, dealing 2d6+2 void damage (DC 18 basic Will save).</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"The Pain of Devotion","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Hunted by Chains is disabled</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The chains rattle ominously, dealing 2d6+2 void damage to all creatures in the haunt (DC 18 basic Will save). The haunt then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-02/athamaru-pirate":{"lang":["Common","Thalassic"],"gear":["Crossbow","Longspear","Scale Mail","Fan Bolts (12)"],"notes":{"speed":"smooth swimmer"},"flavor":"<p>Deep in the sea, schools of athamarus—piscine humanoids armed with spears and specialized crossbows—stalk sharks, sea serpents, and giant squid from the backs of their giant moray eel mounts. The first hunters to strike are armed with barbed harpoons that deploy large fans of seaweed, slowing and exhausting their prey. A daring few athamarus use the embedded harpoon as a handle to ride prey for a short time. Once the creature is tired, remaining hunters finish it with longspears. Athamarus developed this hunting tradition to forge skilled warriors and deter potential attackers, partially in response to centuries of oppression and mistreatment from other aquatic cultures.</p>\n<p>Athamarus rarely hunt land-dwellers, instead offering to trade their services as guides in exchange for metal and ceramic items they can't build underwater—and for tubers, which they consider earthy delicacies. They render aid to damaged sailing ships and rescue shipwrecked sailors, providing food and guidance.</p>\n<p>Athamaru communities—usually villages of 200 individuals or fewer—are matriarchal. The ruler of a given community is also the primary egg-layer, providing each generation with powerful familial bonds. The communities are tight-knit and loyal. Matriarchs are advised and assisted by primal spellcasters and healers.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Diving Reload","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The athamaru pirate can dive underwater, giving them concealment, and reload in the same action.</p>"},{"n":"Fan Bolt","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The athamaru pirate prepares their hooked crossbow bolts with carefully woven seaweed. On a successful crossbow Strike, the bolt embeds and the seaweed fan deploys. The target takes a –10-foot status penalty to its swim Speed. A creature can Interact to attempt a DC 18 Athletics check, removing the bolt on a success.</p>\n<p>Effect: Fan Bolt</p>"},{"n":"Hunt Prey","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate"],"f":"","d":"<p>The athamaru pirate designates a single creature they can see and hear, or one they're Tracking, as their prey. The athamaru pirate gains a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to Seek the prey and to Survival checks to Track the prey. The first time the athamaru pirate hits their designated prey in a round, they deal an additional 1d8 precision damage. These effects last until the pirate uses Hunt Prey again.</p>"},{"n":"Smooth Swimmer","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The athamaru pirate ignores difficult terrain caused by aquatic terrain features.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-02/athamaru-swab":{"lang":["Common","Thalassic"],"gear":["Crossbow","Longspear","Scale Mail","Fan Bolts (12)"],"notes":{"speed":"smooth swimmer"},"flavor":"<p>Deep in the sea, schools of athamarus—piscine humanoids armed with spears and specialized crossbows—stalk sharks, sea serpents, and giant squid from the backs of their giant moray eel mounts. The first hunters to strike are armed with barbed harpoons that deploy large fans of seaweed, slowing and exhausting their prey. A daring few athamarus use the embedded harpoon as a handle to ride prey for a short time. Once the creature is tired, remaining hunters finish it with longspears. Athamarus developed this hunting tradition to forge skilled warriors and deter potential attackers, partially in response to centuries of oppression and mistreatment from other aquatic cultures.</p>\n<p>Athamarus rarely hunt land-dwellers, instead offering to trade their services as guides in exchange for metal and ceramic items they can't build underwater—and for tubers, which they consider earthy delicacies. They render aid to damaged sailing ships and rescue shipwrecked sailors, providing food and guidance.</p>\n<p>Athamaru communities—usually villages of 200 individuals or fewer—are matriarchal. The ruler of a given community is also the primary egg-layer, providing each generation with powerful familial bonds. The communities are tight-knit and loyal. Matriarchs are advised and assisted by primal spellcasters and healers.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Diving Reload","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The athamaru swab can dive underwater, giving them concealment, and reload in the same action.</p>"},{"n":"Fan Bolt","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The athamaru swab prepares their hooked crossbow bolts with carefully woven seaweed. On a successful crossbow Strike, the bolt embeds and the seaweed fan deploys. The target takes a –10-foot status penalty to its swim Speed. A creature can Interact to attempt a DC 18 Athletics check, removing the bolt on a success.</p>\n<p>Effect: Fan Bolt</p>"},{"n":"Hunt Prey","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate"],"f":"","d":"<p>The athamaru swab designates a single creature they can see and hear, or one they're Tracking, as their prey. The athamaru swab gains a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to Seek the prey and to Survival checks to Track the prey. The first time the athamaru swab hits their designated prey in a round, they deal an additional 1d8 precision damage. These effects last until the swab uses Hunt Prey again.</p>"},{"n":"Smooth Swimmer","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The athamaru swab ignores difficult terrain caused by aquatic terrain features.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-01/bartolo-posandi":{"lang":["Common"],"gear":["Longsword","Breastplate"],"abilities":[{"n":"Retributive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An enemy damages Bartolo's ally, and both are within 15 feet of him</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Bartolo protects his ally and strikes his foe. The ally gains resistance 3 to all damage against the triggering damage. If the foe is within reach, Bartolo makes a melee Strike against it.</p>\n<p>Effect: Champion's Resistance</p>"},{"n":"Shield Block (See Living Shield)","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster has its shield raised and takes damage from a physical attack.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster snaps its shield into place to deflect a blow. The shield prevents the monster from taking an amount of damage up to the shield's Hardness. The monster and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.</p></p>"},{"n":"Living Shield","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["attack"],"f":"","d":"<p>Bartolo grapples a creature and uses it as a shield, gaining +2 to his AC and the Shield Block reaction while the target is grabbed. Use the creature's level plus item bonus to AC (if any) as its Hardness.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-01/bartolo-posandi-3-4":{"lang":["Common"],"gear":["Longsword","Breastplate"],"abilities":[{"n":"Retributive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An enemy damages Bartolo's ally, and both are within 15 feet of him</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Bartolo protects his ally and strikes his foe The ally gains resistance 5 to all damage against the triggering damage If the foe is within reach, Bartolo makes a melee Strike against it</p>\n<p>Effect: Champion's Resistance</p>"},{"n":"Shield Block (See Living Shield)","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster has its shield raised and takes damage from a physical attack.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster snaps its shield into place to deflect a blow. The shield prevents the monster from taking an amount of damage up to the shield's Hardness. The monster and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.</p></p>"},{"n":"Living Shield","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["attack"],"f":"","d":"<p>Bartolo grapples a creature and uses it as a shield, gaining +2 to his AC and the Shield Block reaction while the target is grabbed. Use the creature's level plus item bonus to AC (if any) as its Hardness.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-01/bubbling-pile-of-orts":{"description":"<p>A rift to Hell crackles with unstable energy from the broken summoning circle as a squirming mass of fiends struggles to emerge A blood mist projection of a Hellknight angrily commands them.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 19 Arcana, DC 19 Nature, DC 19 Occultism, or DC 19 Religion (2 actions) (trained) while within 15 feet to weaken the rift, dealing 3d4 spirit damage to it. This damage has the holy trait.</p>","routine":"<p>(1 action) The Hellknight commands the orts, and the trap lashes out at each enemy creature in its space and adjacent, dealing 1d10+6 slashing damage (DC 18 basic Reflex save) If no enemy is in reach, an ort emerges in an adjacent square.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Hellfire","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["aura"],"f":"","d":"<p>All orts within 30 feet have +1 status bonus to hit and deal 1d4 extra fire damage on a hit.</p>"},{"n":"Bubble","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The trap receives a critical hit or critically fails a saving throw</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> One ort emerges adjacent.</p>"},{"n":"Planar Breach","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The magic circle is broken</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The pile disgorges orts and then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-02/captain-conziva":{"lang":["Common"],"lore":[["Sailing Lore",11]],"gear":["Dagger","Naval Pike"],"flavor":"<p>A ship's boatswain, or bosun, leads the deckhands who maintain the ship.</p><hr><p>Adventurers may need passage on a swift vessel, or they might face danger from raiders at sea or in coastal settlements.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Captain's Command","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","concentrate","emotion","linguistic","mental"],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Captain Conziva orders an ally to attack or to get in position. Until the end of the ally's next turn, they gain the captain's choice of a +2 status bonus to attack rolls or a +10-foot status bonus to their Speeds.</p>\n<p>Effect: Bosun's Command</p>"},{"n":"Pike and Strike","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Captain Conziva Strikes with her naval pike. If this Strike hits, the captain can either move the target 5 feet within the pike's reach or make a claw Strike against the target without increasing her multiple attack penalty until after the claw Strike.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-19/claws-of-choral":{"lang":["Common","Draconic","Hallit","Skald","Pyric"],"gear":["Maul","Studded Leather Armor"],"flavor":"<p>Criminal organizations are always happy to loan out money at exorbitant rates, and their legbreakers are always happy to collect.</p><hr><p>In the underbelly of society, the lawless reign supreme.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Break Legs!","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The claw makes a maul Strike against an adjacent creature. If it hits, the creature is knocked Prone and becomes Clumsy 1 for 1 minute. As long as this clumsy condition lasts, the creature also takes a –5-foot penalty to its Speeds and has weakness 5 to the claw's Strikes.</p>\n<p>Effect: Break Legs!</p>"},{"n":"Breath of the Dragon","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["fire","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The claw breathes a blast of flame that deals 6d6 fire damage in a 20-foot cone (DC 21 basic Reflex save). The claw can't use Breath of the Dragon again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Stampeding Shove","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The claw Shoves a creature, gaining a +2 circumstance bonus to their Athletics check if the target is Prone. If the Shove succeeds, the target takes 2d10 bludgeoning damage (double damage on a critical success).</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-06/damaged-jaws-of-hell":{"description":"<p>The machine is a cylindrical device ringed in blades with a devilish eye at its center. Gnome inventors created the mechanical device, which taps into the planes of earth and fre to create powerful blasts to damage fortress walls or decimate ranks of enemies. Unfortunately, the many miles of forest have not been kind and it's malfunctioning. The damaged jaws planar connections have weakened to a mere trickle and, when activated, it lashes out in an uncontrolled frenzy. The blades encircling it begin lashing out.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 18 Arcana, DC 18 Crafting, DC 18 Nature, or DC 18 Thievery (trained) twice, to sever the connection to the planes of fre and earth. DC 16 Crafting or DC 16 Thievery (trained) once, to remove the pintle connecting the limber to the horses. A creature must be adjacent to the jaws to make either check.</p>","reset":"<p>The planar connection shuts down after 1 minute. The horses will tire and stop running after 1 minute.</p>","routine":"<p>(three actions) On its turn each round, the horses spend one action to move 30 feet, dragging the limber carrying the jaws behind them in a randomly chosen direction. The horses will not move through other creatures. Players on the limber when it moves must attempt a DC 18 Acrobatics check when it moves or fall of. Removing the pintle will end the random movement. The jaws use 2 actions to Spit Fire or make melee strikes against an adjacent creature.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Jaws Statistics","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Jaws Hardness</strong> 15</p>\n<p><strong>Jaws HP</strong> 60 (BT 30)</p>"},{"n":"Blades of Vengeance","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A Small or larger creature, moves within 10 feet of the jaws.</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> One of the blades lashes out, making one Strike against the creature.</p>"},{"n":"Spit Fire","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The jaws launch a magma ball (range 60 feet, 10-foot burst), randomly, at the largest group of creatures, not including itself, it can catch in the blast dealing 3d4 bludgeoning plus 3d4 fire damage. Each creature caught in the blast must attempt a DC 18 Reflex save. The jaws cannot Spit Fire again for 1d4+1 rounds.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and is knocked Prone.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes double damage, 1 persistent fire damage, and is knocked prone.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-04/diabolic-messenger":{"lang":["Common"],"lore":[["Absalom Court Lore",14]],"gear":["Dagger (4)","Rapier","Leather Armor","Disguise Kit","Clothing (Fine)","Thieves' Toolkit"],"abilities":[{"n":"Hidden Blade","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The diabolic messenger draws a weapon and then Strikes with it The target of the Strike is Off-Guard against the attack.</p>"},{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The diabolic messenger deals an extra 1d6 precision damage to Off-Guard creatures.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-07/distracted-zaluraak":{"lang":["Common","Draconic"],"lore":[["Accounting Lore",18],["Mercantile Lore",18]],"notes":{"saves":"+2 status to all saves vs. arcane"},"flavor":"<p>Fortune dragons have the innate ability to draw upon the raw magical energies that surround them. They constantly use these magical energies to empower their magical abilities and even their bodies, as the energy can heal wounds. A fortune dragon has a typical build for an arcane dragon, but their bodies sport a striking feature: their treasure. The dragon's nature of drawing upon magic causes coins, gems, and, most notably, magical items to cling to their body like iron drawn to magnets. A dragon constantly pulls magical energies from the items attached to their body and makes use of these energies to cast spells. The magical energies that flow through a fortune dragon constantly flow through the dragon's items as well, and in many cases, the items melt from the heat produced in this process. Fortune dragons are seekers of novel experiences. This desire for originality leads fortune dragons to approach visitors of other ancestries with curiosity, though this initial interest quickly wanes if a visitor lacks exciting qualities.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Dragons come in myriad forms, with many having magical abilities or connections to magic. Some dragons draw greater power from magic than others, allowing them to manifest abilities or alter their physiques with prolonged exposure to magic. These dragons become more powerful as they age and strengthen their connections with their magical origins. Scholars debate the classification of these dragons, with some preferring the name magical dragons and others using traditional dragons due to their connection to specific magical traditions. Regardless of their names, these dragons share a number of characteristics: their ability to tap into magical energies, intensified might and cunning as they grow older, and an inclination to hoard vast amounts of treasure and wealth.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"+2 Status to All Saves vs. Arcane","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Capture Spell","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["arcane"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The dragon succeeds or critically succeeds on a saving throw against a spell</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The dragon attempts to capture a portion of the spell's magic to feed themself. They attempt to counteract the spell (counteract rank 5, counteract modifier +20). If successful, the dragon is unaffected by the spell and regains one expended spontaneous spell slot; other subjects are affected by the spell normally.</p>"},{"n":"Disruptive Breath","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","force"],"f":"","d":"<p>The dragon unleashes a spray of magic-disrupting energies that deals 7d6 force damage in a 30-foot cone (DC 27 basic Reflex save). Creatures that fail become Stupefied 1 (Stupefied 2 on a critical failure) for 1 minute.</p>\n<p>The dragon can't use Disruptive Breath again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Draconic Frenzy","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The dragon makes two claw Strikes and one tail Strike in any order.</p>"},{"n":"Draconic Momentum","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Whenever they score a critical hit with a Strike, the dragon chooses to either recharge Disruptive Breath or regain one expended spontaneous spell slot.</p>"},{"n":"Share the Wealth","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The dragon's body is covered in riches (this is typically the case when the dragon is first encountered)</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The dragon shakes their body aggressively, sending coins and other riches flying in every direction, dealing 7d6 bludgeoning damage with a DC 26 basic Reflex save to all creatures in a 30-foot emanation. The dragon's body is then no longer covered in riches.</p>"},{"n":"Treasure Dive","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The dragon's body isn't covered in riches and the dragon is adjacent to their hoard</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The dragon Strides or Burrows through their hoard using their land Speed. They coat themself in coins, magic items, and other treasures. This contact with magical items revitalizes the dragon, causing them to regain one expended spontaneous spell slot.</p>\n<p>The dragon can move through other creatures while moving in this way. Creatures in the dragon's path, or above it if the dragon Burrows, must succeed at a DC 24 Reflex save or be pushed 10 feet (or pushed 20 feet and knocked Prone on a critical failure).</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-03/dragged-to-the-briny-depths":{"description":"<p>A giant squid rams the ship from below, using its beak to puncture the hull. It then wraps its tentacles around the mast, rocking the ship violently.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 23 Athletics to pull the tentacles from the mast, stopping the ship from rocking; two total successes are required to disable the hazard.</p>","reset":"<p>The squid releases the ship for one round before regripping the mast and resetting the hazard The hazard no longer resets once the PCs defeat the naiads or they flee</p>","routine":"<p>(two actions) On its initiative, the squid uses its first action to pull on the mast Every creature must attempt a DC 22 Reflex save On a failure, it falls Prone If a creature is prone when attempting the save, it slides 10 feet in a direction determined by the GM on a failure If this movement would force a creature off the ship, it can attempt to Grab an Edge The squid uses its second action to make one tentacle attack</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Flip the Ship","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The naiads board the ship</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Each creature standing on the deck must attempt a DC 22 Reflex save or fall Prone. The hazard then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-03/dragged-to-the-depths":{"description":"<p>A giant squid rams the ship from below, using its beak to puncture the hull. It then wraps its tentacles around the mast, rocking the ship violently.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 20 Athletics to pull the tentacles from the mast, stopping the ship from rocking; two total successes are required to disable the hazard.</p>","reset":"<p>The squid releases the ship for one round before regripping the mast and resetting the hazard The hazard no longer resets once the PCs defeat the naiads or they flee</p>","routine":"<p>(two actions) On its initiative, the squid uses its first action to pull on the mast Every creature must attempt a DC 20 Reflex save On a failure, it falls Prone If a creature is prone when attempting the save, it slides 10 feet in a direction determined by the GM on a failure If this movement would force a creature off the ship, it can attempt to Grab an Edge The squid uses its second action to make one tentacle attack</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Flip the Ship","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The naiads board the ship</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Each creature standing on the deck must attempt a DC 20 Reflex save or fall Prone. The hazard then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-07/dragons-ward":{"disable":"<p>DC 27 Thievery (master) to painstakingly remove the rune without triggering the magic, or Dispel Magic (4th rank; counteract DC 25) to counteract the rune.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(expert)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Curse the Intruders","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["curse","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature passes the threshold</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Each living creature within 30 feet must succeed at a DC 23 Will save or be subjected to the dragon's curse A cursed creature takes a –2 status penalty to Fortitude saves, and any natural or magical healing it receives is halved The curse remains until removed by Cleanse Affliction or similar magic</p>\n<p>Effect: Curse the Intruders</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-08/dutys-soulshackle":{"description":"<p>A length of humanoid spine is held into a staff by the hooked chain embedded in and entwined around it. Additional spectral chains of pure shadowstuff hold it aloft and sinuously surround it.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 20 Arcana, DC 20 Occultism, or DC 20 Religion (trained) to disrupt the spectral energies channeled by the intelligent item. Each success reduces the haunt's actions by one. When the haunt has no more actions, it is disabled.</p>","routine":"<p>(three actions) On its initiative, Duty's Soulshackle first uses Call to Serve if it's able to and spends any remaining actions making velstrac chains Strikes against its enemies.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(expert); noticing the staff has a DC of 0.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Chained by Duty","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Lyari proposes how to free herself from <em>Duty's Soulshackle</em>.</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> <em>Duty's Soulshackle</em> quivers in rage before unleashing more spectral chains. The haunt then rolls initiative.</p>"},{"n":"Call to Serve","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><em>Duty's Soulshackle</em> creates a Withered Leaf of Talhindir within 10 feet of itself. It then cannot use this action for 1d6 rounds.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-08/dutys-soulshackle-3-4":{"description":"<p>A length of humanoid spine is held into a staff by the hooked chain embedded in and entwined around it. Additional spectral chains of pure shadowstuff hold it aloft and sinuously surround it.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 23 Arcana, DC 23 Occultism, or DC 23 Religion (trained) to disrupt the spectral energies channeled by the intelligent item. Each success reduces the haunt's actions by one. When the haunt has no more actions, it is disabled.</p>","routine":"<p>(three actions) On its initiative, Duty's Soulshackle first uses Call to Serve if it's able to and spends any remaining actions making velstrac chains Strikes against its enemies.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(expert); noticing the staff has a DC of 0.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Chained by Duty","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Lyari proposes how to free herself from <em>Duty's Soulshackle</em>.</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> <em>Duty's Soulshackle</em> quivers in rage before unleashing more spectral chains. The haunt then rolls initiative.</p>"},{"n":"Call to Serve","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><em>Duty's Soulshackle</em> creates a Shriveled Leaf of Talhindir within 10 feet of itself. It then cannot use this action for 1d6 rounds.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-03/enraged-sea-life":{"description":"<p>A swarm of aggressive cuttlefish, octopuses, devil rays, and countless other species of sea life bite and bludgeon Timonithaea's enemies.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 23 Thievery (trained) to remove the crown from the altar while avoiding being bitten by the swarming sea life; or Dispel Magic (3rd rank; counteract DC 23) to disable the crown's enchantment, breaking Timonithaea's control over the sea creatures.</p>","routine":"<p>(one action) The sea creatures attack, dealing 1d8+3 bludgeoning plus 1d8+3 piercing damage to each creature hostile to Timonithaea within the temple (DC 22 basic Reflex save).</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Aquatic Onslaught","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The PCs enter the main temple chamber</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The chamber fills with sea creatures, then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-19/eye-of-choral":{"lang":["Common","Draconic","Hallit","Skald","Pyric"],"lore":[["Brevoy Lore",15],["House Rogarvia Lore",20],["Library Lore",20]],"notes":{"per":"key sense, smoke vision"},"abilities":[{"n":"Frightful Presence","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>90 feet. DC 23 Will</p><hr><p><p>A creature that first enters the area must attempt a Will save.</p>\n<p>Regardless of the result of the saving throw, the creature is temporarily immune to this monster's Frightful Presence for 1 minute.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected by the presence.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Frightened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 2.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 4.</p></p>"},{"n":"Key Sense","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["detection"],"f":"","d":"<p>The Eye of Choral was created alongside several magical keys. It can sense the presence of these keys anywhere in Rahasia Rinca, communicate telepathically with anyone bearing a key within the complex, and always knows whether a creature possesses such a key.</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike (Jaws Only)","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Shadow Construct","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["illusion"],"f":"","d":"<p>The Eye of Choral is only semi-real. The first time each round a PC is hit by one of the Eye's Strikes, the creature makes a DC 23 Will save to realize the creature's attacks aren't wholly real. The result applies to the damage of that Strike and lasts until the start of the creature's next turn.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature gains resistance to damage from the Eye's Strikes equal to its level.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature gains resistance to damage from the Eye's Strikes equal to half its level.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is affected by the Eye's Strikes as normal.</p>"},{"n":"Draconic Frenzy","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The Eye makes two claw Strikes and one wing Strike in any order</p>"},{"n":"Draconic Momentum","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The Eye recharges their Pyre Breath whenever they score a critical hit with a Strike.</p>"},{"n":"Pyre Breath","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["fire","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The Eye breathes a blast of flame that deals 7d6 fire damage in a 40-foot cone (DC 23 basic Reflex save). Creatures that critically fail their save catch fire, taking 1d6 persistent fire damage. The area then fills with black smoke for 1 minute. This has the effects of mist, except it fills the cone's area. The Eye can't use Pyre Breath again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Stoke the Flames","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["fire","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The Eye intensifies nearby fires. Every foe within 60 feet that is taking persistent fire damage takes 2d6 fire damage.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-15/falling-decorations":{"description":"<p>Large metal moons and spears break apart and fall when a creature moves beneath them.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 28 Thievery (expert) or DC 28 Crafting (expert) to prevent the decorations from falling.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(expert) to notice the incipient collapse; noticing the decorations has a DC of 0.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"The Sky is Falling","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature walks through the space under the hanging decorations</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The little bit of disturbance is all the cracked decorations need to come dislodged. They fall, their sharp metal edges dealing 6d10+15 piercing damage (DC 28 basic Reflex save) to those underneath them.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-20/fiendish-hospitality":{"description":"<p>A haunting voice from the statue of a woman in servant's garb calls out to those in sight, welcoming them to stay. The statue then changes to the image of a gylou devil.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 14 Religion (trained) to disrupt the unholy energy projecting from the statue, DC 17 Athletics to knock the statue off balance Three total successes using either skill disables the hazard.</p>","reset":"<p>The statue returns to its human visage once no creatures are in the courtyard and it resets after 1d4+1 rounds. Until it resets, a creature can destroy the statue with a DC 16 Athletics check, permanently disabling the hazard.</p>","routine":"<p>(two actions) For its first action, the statue uses handmaiden's command. With its second action, it makes a stony tentacle Strike at the closest target within range; if there are no targets, the trap instead uses handmaiden's command again.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Ordered Escort","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["divine","mental","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A non-devil triggers or disables the slamming door hazard</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The statue takes on the visage of a handmaiden devil as a wave of unholy energy washes over the courtyard. Each creature in the courtyard must succeed at a DC 17 Will save or be Slowed 1 for as long as it remains in the courtyard. The trap then rolls initiative.</p>"},{"n":"Handmaiden's Command","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","divine","mental","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>The statue emits a supernaturally compelling command. Each creature in the courtyard must make a DC 17 Will save, with results below.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is pulled 5 feet toward the statue.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is pulled 5 feet toward the statue and must spend the first action on its next turn making a Step toward the statue.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-03/frenzied-sea-life":{"description":"<p>A swarm of aggressive cuttlefish, octopuses, devil rays, and countless other species of sea life bite and bludgeon Timonithaea's enemies.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 27 Thievery (trained) to remove the crown from the altar while avoiding being bitten by the swarming sea life, or Dispel Magic (4th rank; counteract DC 27) to disable the crown's enchantment, breaking Timonithaea's control over the sea creatures.</p>","routine":"<p>(one action) The sea creatures attack, dealing 1d10+4 bludgeoning plus 1d10+4 piercing damage to each creature hostile to Timonithaea within the temple (DC 25 basic Reflex save).</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Aquatic Onslaught","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The PCs enter the main temple chamber</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The chamber fills with sea creatures, then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-11/gloom-bulwark":{"lang":["Arboreal","Can't speak any language"],"abilities":[{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Thicken","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The bulwark is targeted with a melee or ranged attack by an attacker it can see</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The bulwark gains resistance 10 against the triggering attack, but takes a –10-foot status penalty to all its Speeds until the end of its next turn.</p>"},{"n":"Constrict","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>2d8+3 bludgeoning, DC 23 basic Fortitude</p><hr><p><p>The monster deals the listed amount of damage to any number of creatures Grabbed or Restrained by it. Each of those creatures can attempt a basic Fortitude save with the listed DC.</p></p>"},{"n":"Stench","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["olfactory"],"f":"","d":"<p>The creature must attempt a DC 24 Fortitude save. On a failure, the creature is Sickened 1, and on a critical failure, the creature is also Enfeebled 1 for as long as it is sickened. A creature that succeeds at its save is temporarily immune to this ability for 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-02/goblin-rigger":{"lang":["Common","Goblin"],"gear":["Shortbow","Scimitar","Leather Armor","Arrows (20)"],"flavor":"<p>The theoretical leaders of goblin raids are called goblin commandos. In practice, goblin commandos rarely continue to lead their comrades once a battle has begun. Most shirk their responsibilities in favor of wading into the fray and claiming more glory from their tribe-mates.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>These small humanoids typically have green or gray skin and large heads with wide ears. While some goblins are civilized and have worked hard to be considered upstanding members of humanoid communities, many are impetuous and vicious creatures who delight in wreaking havoc. These goblins think nothing of slaughtering livestock, stealing, or burning down a building purely for momentary delight. They revel in playing malicious tricks on taller humanoids, whom they call \"longshanks.\"</p>\n<p>Goblins are superstitious, with an intense awe of magic and a fascination with fire; goblins who master magic or fire earn great respect from their kin. Most other humanoids find it difficult to understand goblins' outlook: they hate canines but eagerly share their lairs with so-called \"goblin dogs,\" they fearlessly attack larger creatures but are terrified of horses, and they despise vegetables yet consider pickles a delicacy. To a goblin, of course, these are all perfectly sensible life choices.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Goblin Scuttle","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An ally ends a move action adjacent to the rigger</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The goblin rigger Steps.</p>"},{"n":"Boarding Action","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The goblin rigger swings on a rope or Strides, moving up to double their Speed. If the rigger boarded or disembarked a boat during this movement, they can make a melee Strike at the end of their movement that deals one extra damage die on a hit.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-07/greater-demonologist":{"lang":["Chthonian","Common"],"lore":[["Academia Lore",17],["Demon Lore",21]],"gear":["Longspear","Robes","Fiendish Hypotheses and Protections from Same (Spellbook)"],"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>Demonologists can pull a creature from the Outer Rifts and bend it to their will... for a time.</p><hr><p>Hidden secrets and occult powers have an irresistible lure for many. Since the majority of these NPCs are spellcasters, consider using alternative spell lists to adjust their themes.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Demonic Temptation","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["divine","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>Demonic study has garnered the attention of at least one demon who is actively trying to possess the demonologist. When the demonologist publicly espouses the benefits of demonic power (whether they believe it a good thing or not), they gain a +1 status bonus to skill checks, AC, and saves for 1 day. These bonuses don't apply against demons. At the end of the day, the demonologist must attempt a DC 20 Will save, becoming possessed for 1 day on a failure (or permanently on a critical failure).</p>"},{"n":"Breach the Outer Rifts","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The demonologist's last action was to cast a non-cantrip spell</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The demonologist siphons energy drawn from the Outer Rifts into their weapon. Until the end of the turn, the weapon deals an extra 2d6 damage.</p>\n<p>Roll 1d20 to determine the type:</p><ul><li>1–7 acid</li><li>8–9 cold</li><li>10–11 electricity</li><li>12–18 fire</li><li>19–20 void.</li></ul>"},{"n":"Demon Summoning","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The demonologist can cast a 5th-rank Summon Fiend arcane spell to summon a demon. To do so, they must sacrifice two 4th-rank prepared spells and voluntarily take 4d12 mental damage that can't be reduced or prevented. If the demonologist is unable to Sustain the Spell, including if they're knocked out or killed, the spell continues, but the GM rolls a DC 10 Flat each round, ending the spell on a failure.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-07/greater-dragons-ward":{"disable":"<p>DC 30 Thievery (master) to painstakingly remove the rune without triggering the magic, or Dispel Magic (4th rank; counteract DC 28) to counteract the rune.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(expert)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Curse the Intruders","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["curse","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature passes the threshold</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Each living creature within 30 feet must succeed at a DC 26 Will save or be subjected to the dragon's curse A cursed creature takes a –2 status penalty to Fortitude saves, and any natural or magical healing it receives is halved The curse remains until removed by Cleanse Affliction or similar magic</p>\n<p>Effect: Curse the Intruders</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-11/heart-of-gloom":{"description":"<p>Within this mockery of a tree is a large, beating growth pushing grotesque branches through jagged planar fssures.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 25 Arcana or DC 25 Occultism to close of a planar breach, DC 21 Athletics to snap one of the branches, or 4th-rank Planar Tether to seal of a breach. For each branch snapped or breach sealed, remove one action from the Heart's routine. Once the Heart reaches 0 actions in its routine, it is disabled.</p>","reset":"<p>The trap deactivates and resets after 1 minute<strong>.</strong></p>","routine":"<p>(3 actions) The Heart spends all of its actions making thorny vine Strikes against different creatures. The Heart doesn't take a multiple attack penalty.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(expert) to detect the fraying planes around it; noticing the Heart has a DC of 0</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Crushing Horror","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The Heart breaks its planar bonds</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Each creature in the area must attempt a DC 22 Will save. The Heart then rolls initiative.</p><hr><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature shrugs of the infuence of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes 3d8 mental damage and is Frightened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes 6d8 mental damage and is Frightened 2. The creature can't reduce its frightened value below 1 for 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Anguish","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The vine squeezes and overwhelms the creature with fear. The target takes 4d4 mental damage with a DC 24 basic Will save. On a critical failure, the creature is also Frightened 1 and can't reduce its frightened value below 1 for 1 minute.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-06/heavily-damaged-jaws-of-hell":{"description":"<p>The machine is a cylindrical device ringed in blades with a devilish eye at its center. Gnome inventors created the mechanical device, which taps into the planes of earth and fre to create powerful blasts to damage fortress walls or decimate ranks of enemies. Unfortunately, the many miles of forest have not been kind and it's malfunctioning. The damaged jaws planar connections have weakened to a mere trickle and, when activated, it lashes out in an uncontrolled frenzy. The blades encircling it begin lashing out.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 15 Arcana, DC 15 Crafting, DC 15 Nature, or DC 15 Thievery (trained) twice, to sever the connection to the planes of fre and earth. DC 13 Crafting or DC 13 Thievery (trained) once, to remove the pintle connecting the limber to the horses. A creature must be adjacent to the jaws to make either check.</p>","reset":"<p>The planar connection shuts down after 1 minute. The horses will tire and stop running after 1 minute.</p>","routine":"<p>(three actions) On its turn each round, the horses spend one action to move 30 feet, dragging the limber carrying the jaws behind them in a randomly chosen direction. The horses will not move through other creatures. Players on the limber when it moves must attempt a DC 15 Acrobatics check when it moves or fall of. Removing the pintle will end the random movement. The jaws use 2 actions to Spit Fire or make melee strikes against an adjacent creature.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Jaws Statistics","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Jaws Hardness</strong> 8</p>\n<p><strong>Jaws HP</strong> 30 (BT 15)</p>"},{"n":"Blades of Vengeance","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A Small or larger creature, moves within 10 feet of the jaws.</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> One of the blades lashes out, making one Strike against the creature.</p>"},{"n":"Spit Fire","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The jaws launch a magma ball (range 60 feet, 10-foot burst), randomly, at the largest group of creatures, not including itself, it can catch in the blast dealing 2d4 bludgeoning plus 2d4 fire damage. Each creature caught in the blast must attempt a DC 15 Reflex save. The jaws cannot Spit Fire again for 1d4+1 rounds.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and is knocked Prone.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes double damage, 1 persistent fire damage, and is knocked prone.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-14/howling-terror":{"abilities":[{"n":"Hellfire Strikes","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature critically hit by a howling terror's Strike takes 1d6 persistent fire damage.</p>"},{"n":"Metallically Infused","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The howling terror is a horrible conglomeration of a metal elemental and an animal infused with diabolic power. Its Strikes and Molten Metal Rain count as whichever metal is most advantageous for the howling terror</p>"},{"n":"Molten Metal Rain","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["magical","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per minute</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The howling terror launches a torrent of molten metal in a 10-foot burst within 100 feet. The burst deals 3d6 bludgeoning damage and 2d6 fire damage with a Basic DC 21 Reflex save. Creatures that enter the area or start their turn there take 1 fire damage until the metal cools after 5 rounds.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-08/hunted-by-chains":{"description":"<p>Shadowy chains reach out to ensnare creatures trapped in the mindscape.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 17 Acrobatics to avoid the chains, or DC 17 Arcana, DC 17 Occultism, or DC 17 Religion to ritually disrupt the haunting. Each success reduces the haunt's actions by one. When the haunt has no more actions, it is disabled and the Scaling the Chain haunt triggers.</p>","reset":"<p>The haunt resets the next time the <em>Soulshackle</em> traps creatures in the library.</p>","routine":"<p>(two actions) Spectral chains snake out to wrap around three different random creatures trapped in the haunt, who must each succeed at a DC 16 Reflex save or have the Restrained condition until it Escapes. Each round that a creature starts its turn Grabbed, it takes 2d4 nonlethal force damage. Spectral scars form on any creature knocked Unconscious by this haunt.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Chains of Undeath","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Talhindir's Autumn is disabled</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> A spectral image of Duty's Soulshackle appears in a display nook, snaking out chains of dark energy toward each creature. Each living creature in the haunt must attempt a DC 16 Will save or be Frightened 1 The haunt then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-08/hunted-by-dutys-bonds":{"description":"<p>Shadowy chains reach out to ensnare creatures trapped in the mindscape.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 18 Acrobatics to avoid the chains, or DC 18 Arcana, DC 18 Occultism, or DC 18 Religion to ritually disrupt the haunting. Each success reduces the haunt's actions by one. When the haunt has no more actions, it is disabled and the Scaling the Chain haunt triggers.</p>","reset":"<p>The haunt resets the next time the <em>Soulshackle</em> traps creatures in the library.</p>","routine":"<p>(two actions) Spectral chains snake out to wrap around three different random creatures trapped in the haunt, who must each succeed at a DC 17 Reflex save or have the Restrained condition until it Escapes. Each round that a creature starts its turn Grabbed, it takes 2d4+1 nonlethal force damage. Spectral scars form on any creature knocked Unconscious by this haunt.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Chains of Undeath","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Talhindir's Autumn is disabled</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> A spectral image of Duty's Soulshackle appears in a display nook, snaking out chains of dark energy toward each creature. Each living creature in the haunt must attempt a DC 16 Will save or be Frightened 1 The haunt then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-01/imp-minion":{"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>Imps are fiendish infiltrators and corrupters who, despite their diminutive stature, are more than capable of subtly influencing a weak-willed individual into performing increasingly evil acts over time. An imp will often agree to serve a mortal and act docile and loyal in a long-term plot to eventually get their master killed or damn their soul. Imps are born directly from the Outer Planes themselves, rather than from mortal souls, and thus they serve outside any fiendish hierarchies, granting them leeway to pursue their specialties. Despite standing a mere 2 feet tall, imps can be vicious combatants, flying out of reach and turning invisible to escape should the odds turn against them.</p>"},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-01/imp-minion-3-4":{"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>Imps are fiendish infiltrators and corrupters who, despite their diminutive stature, are more than capable of subtly influencing a weak-willed individual into performing increasingly evil acts over time. An imp will often agree to serve a mortal and act docile and loyal in a long-term plot to eventually get their master killed or damn their soul. Imps are born directly from the Outer Planes themselves, rather than from mortal souls, and thus they serve outside any fiendish hierarchies, granting them leeway to pursue their specialties. Despite standing a mere 2 feet tall, imps can be vicious combatants, flying out of reach and turning invisible to escape should the odds turn against them.</p>"},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-01/in-a-pickle":{"description":"<p>A soot-blackened brazier glows with fiendish light, shadows fickering inside.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 18 Arcana, DC 18 Occultism, or DC 18 Religion while within 15 feet of the brazier to command it to stop, reducing its actions by 1 (or 2 on a critical success); DC 20 Thievery to fnd the hidden switch on the brazier that deactivates it; or 1st-rank spell, counteract DC 17, to dispel the shadow flames in one square, using any spell with the water or light traits.</p>","reset":"<p>The flames cease 1 minute after all living creatures leave the area, but after 1 hour, a well of darkness fills the brazier and it is ready to trigger again.</p>","routine":"<p>(4 actions) The trap ignites shadowy flames in a 5-foot square within the area of the room A creature that moves into or ends its turn in this fire takes 1d6+5 fire damage (DC 17 basic Fortitude) Increase the DC by 2 if the creature is in magical darkness (DC 19 basic Fortitude).</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Flames of Caina","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["darkness"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A living creature enters the area</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Shadows roil in the brazier. It casts Darkness on itself, and then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-01/in-a-right-pickle":{"description":"<p>A soot-blackened brazier glows with fiendish light, shadows fickering inside.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 21 Arcana, DC 21 Occultism, or DC 21 Religion while within 15 feet of the brazier to command it to stop, reducing its actions by 1 (or 2 on a critical success); DC 23 Thievery to find the hidden switch on the brazier that deactivates it; or 1st-rank spell, counteract DC 20, to dispel the shadow flames in one square, using any spell with the water or light traits</p>","reset":"<p>The flames cease 1 minute after all living creatures leave the area, but after 1 hour, a well of darkness fills the brazier and it is ready to trigger again.</p>","routine":"<p>(4 actions) The trap ignites shadowy flames in a 5-foot square within the area of the room. A creature that moves into or ends its turn in this fire takes 2d6+5 fire damage (DC 19 basic Fortitude save). Increase the DC by 2 if the creature is in magical darkness (DC 21 basic Fortitude).</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Flames of Caina","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["darkness"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A living creature enters the area</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Shadows roil in the brazier. It casts Darkness on itself, and then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-21/infested-attendant":{"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"flavor":"<p>Glowing with a dull amber light, these odious creatures spawn from a combination of baleful magic and fire. These destructive creations sow chaos and demolish fortifications, making them the bane of besieged cities.</p><hr><p>Necromancers most often create these mindless undead as obedient, expendable servitors. Left to its own devices, a zombie seeks only to consume the living, stopping only when its rotting body can no longer hold together.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Slow","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A sulfur zombie is permanently Slowed 1 and can't use reactions.</p>"},{"n":"Death Throes","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a sulfur zombie dies, its body explodes in a 30-foot burst of fire and debris that deals 2d10 bludgeoning plus 2d10 piercing to each creature in the area (DC 21 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Blinding Sulfur","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["incapacitation"],"f":"","d":"<p>A sulfur zombie burns with putrid inner fire. A creature hit by a sulfur zombie's fist Strike must attempt a DC 22 Fortitude save. On a failure, the creature is Blinded for 1 round, or for 1 minute on a critical failure.</p>"},{"n":"Infested","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The zombie is filled with squirming rust-red beetles as well as alchemical sulfur, not fire. It loses the immunity to fire, and its Death Throes and fist Strikes deal piercing damage in place of fire damage.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/quests/kalagemmon-decayed-cyclops":{"lang":["Common","Jotun","Necril"],"gear":["Morningstar"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"focus":1,"abilities":[{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/quests/kalagemmon-decayed-resentment-witch":{"lang":["Common","Jotun","Necril"],"gear":["Morningstar"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"focus":1,"abilities":[{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-02/king-pirate-gorilla":{"flavor":"<p>Gorillas can be territorial creatures, particularly if provoked by hunters or the presence of more dangerous monsters. A gorilla uses its fangs and powerful arms to bite and pummel trespassers with wild abandon.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>While many apes exhibit peaceful or reclusive behavior, gorillas can be territorial, and the megaprimatus is especially aggressive and dangerous.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Boarding Action","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The pirate gorilla swings on a rope or Strides, moving up to double their Speed. If the pirate boarded or disembarked a boat during this movement, they can make a melee Strike at the end of their movement that deals one extra damage die on a hit.</p>"},{"n":"Frightening Display","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The gorilla beats its chest in a terrifying display. Creatures within 30 feet must attempt a DC 20 Will save. While a creature is frightened by this ability, it is Off-Guard to the gorilla.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> No effect and temporarily immune for 1 minute.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 2.</p>"},{"n":"Well-Trained","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The pirate gorilla is used to taking orders on board the ship. It loses its immunity to linguistic efects, including appeals to surrender.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-05/kizrech":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Telepathy 100 feet"],"lore":[["Warfare Lore",19]],"gear":["Trident","Steel Shield","Breastplate","Charm of Cold Resistance"],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"focus":1,"abilities":[{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Infernal Command","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An enemy within 30 feet of Kizrech damages them or their mount</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Kizrech commands their enemy to kneel before them. The triggering enemy must choose to either drop Prone as a free action or take 3d6 mental damage.</p>"},{"n":"Mounted Force","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>While mounted on a fend, Kizrech's trident gains the jousting 1d8 and thrown 60 feet traits, and Kizrech and their mount each increase their level by 1 when resolving incapacitation efects.</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Shield Block","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster has its shield raised and takes damage from a physical attack.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster snaps its shield into place to deflect a blow. The shield prevents the monster from taking an amount of damage up to the shield's Hardness. The monster and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.</p></p>\n<p>Kizrech may use this reaction to prevent their mount from taking damage instead of themself, following the normal rules for Shield Block.</p>"},{"n":"Burning Hoofprints","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["divine","fire","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>Kizrech Strides, trailing hoofprints in each square they exit. The hoofprints burn for 1 minute. A creature on the ground that enters a square with burning hoofprints or begins its turn in one takes 1d6 fire damage. Kizrech can use this ability while mounted, afecting up to 30 feet of contiguous hoofprints from their mount's Stride; this trail is 10 feet wide for a Large mount, or 15 feet wide for a Huge mount.</p>"},{"n":"Trident of Dis","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Kizrech makes a trident Strike, increasing their reach to 10 feet for that Strike. If there is an unholy ally between Kizrech and their target, or if Kizrech is mounted on an unholy creature, that creature's energy causes the Strike to deal an additional 1d8 spirit damage.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-05/kizrech-11-12":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Telepathy 100 feet"],"lore":[["Warfare Lore",22]],"gear":["Trident","Steel Shield","Breastplate","Charm of Cold Resistance"],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"focus":1,"abilities":[{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Infernal Command","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An enemy within 30 feet of Kizrech damages them or their mount</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Kizrech commands their enemy to kneel before them. The triggering enemy must choose to either drop Prone as a free action or take 3d6 mental damage.</p>"},{"n":"Mounted Force","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>While mounted on a fend, Kizrech's trident gains the jousting 1d8 and thrown 60 feet traits, and Kizrech and their mount each increase their level by 1 when resolving incapacitation efects.</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Shield Block","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster has its shield raised and takes damage from a physical attack.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster snaps its shield into place to deflect a blow. The shield prevents the monster from taking an amount of damage up to the shield's Hardness. The monster and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.</p></p>\n<p>Kizrech may use this reaction to prevent their mount from taking damage instead of themself, following the normal rules for Shield Block.</p>"},{"n":"Burning Hoofprints","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["divine","fire","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>Kizrech Strides, trailing hoofprints in each square they exit. The hoofprints burn for 1 minute. A creature on the ground that enters a square with burning hoofprints or begins its turn in one takes 1d8 fire damage. Kizrech can use this ability while mounted, afecting up to 30 feet of contiguous hoofprints from their mount's Stride; this trail is 10 feet wide for a Large mount, or 15 feet wide for a Huge mount.</p>"},{"n":"Trident of Dis","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Kizrech makes a trident Strike, increasing their reach to 10 feet for that Strike. If there is an unholy ally between Kizrech and their target, or if Kizrech is mounted on an unholy creature, that creature's energy causes the Strike to deal an additional 1d8 spirit damage.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-22/kizrech-7-22":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Telepathy 100 feet"],"lore":[["Warfare Lore",13]],"gear":["Trident","Steel Shield","Breastplate","Charm of Cold Resistance"],"notes":{"ac":"(33 with shield raised)","saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>The vast city of Dis trains endless legions of vordines to guard the upper layers of Hell and march across the planes at the archdevils' orders. Although quick to bend their knees to higher-ranking devils and even mortals favored by Asmodeus, vordines are relentlessly cruel to orts and other devils they can call their subordinates.</p>\n<p>Although higher ranks in the infernal military are held by more powerful devils, like the nessari who serve as generals, a labyrinthine structure gives each vordine a rank and certain responsibilities. Some vordines are responsible for the battlefield command of squads, while others relay orders from above or are set to handling specific administrative tasks for their unit. The greatest gift one can offer a vordine is an increased rank to lord over other vordines.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Masters of corruption and architects of conquest, devils seek both to tempt mortal life to join in their pursuit of all things profane and to spread tyranny throughout all worlds. The temptations they offer mortals range from great powers granted by the signing of an infernal contract to twisted favors following a whispered pledge to a diabolic patron, or any number of even subtler exchanges. Those who succumb to these temptations find themselves consigned to an afterlife of endless torment in the pits of Hell, wherein the only hope of escape lies in the chance of being promoted to become a devil in the infernal ranks.</p>\n<p>Every devil has a specific role to play in the upkeep of the remorseless bureaucratic machine that is Hell, from soldiers and scholars to inquisitors, lawyers, judges, and executioners. Lowly orts perform subservient labor to more powerful and specialized devils, such as infantry and contract devils, while the greatest nessaris command entire infernal armies.</p>\n<p>Asmodeus stands at the apex of the structure he created, but the layers below him are marked by a constant jockeying for position. Most diabolic plans ultimately serve to improve the schemer's place in the hierarchy.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Greater Darkvision","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with greater darkvision can see perfectly well in areas of darkness and dim light, though such vision is in black and white only. A creature with greater darkvision can see through even forms of magical darkness.</p></p>"},{"n":"Telepathy 100 feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["aura","magical","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A monster with telepathy can communicate mentally with any creatures within the listed radius, as long as they share a language. This doesn't give any special access to their thoughts, and communicates no more information than normal speech would.</p></p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Infernal Command","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An enemy within 30 feet of Kizrech damages them</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Kizrech commands their enemy to kneel before them. The triggering enemy must choose to either drop Prone as a free action or take 3d6 mental damage.</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Shield Block","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster has its shield raised and takes damage from a physical attack.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster snaps its shield into place to deflect a blow. The shield prevents the monster from taking an amount of damage up to the shield's Hardness. The monster and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.</p></p>"},{"n":"Burning Hoofprints","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["divine","fire","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>Kizrech Strides, trailing hoofprints in each square they exit. The hoofprints burn for 1 minute. A creature on the ground that enters a square with burning hoofprints or begins its turn in one takes 1d8 fire damage.</p>"},{"n":"Trident of Dis","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Kizrech makes a trident Strike, increasing their reach to 10 feet for that Strike If there is an unholy ally between Kizrech and their target, or if Kizrech is leading a troop, unholy energy causes the Strike to deal an additional 1d8 spirit damage.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-07/lesser-marsh-giant":{"lang":["Aklo","Common","Jotun","Thalassic"],"gear":["Gaff"],"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>Dwellers of brackish coastal salt marshes and fetid bogs and swamps, marsh giants appear hideous to most airbreathers, with fishlike mouths, slimy graygreen skin, and dark, beady eyes. They prefer to eat the flesh of those they slay in battle, including other marsh giants, and guzzle stagnant water from cauldrons or directly from their swampy homes.</p>\n<p>Marsh giant clans are insular, with each clan dedicating itself to zealous worship of a sea-dwelling deity, demon lord, or stranger entity. Whatever forces call to the marsh giants sometimes ensnare boggards and ogres as well, gathering in grim worship. Rather than favor these humanoid hangerson, marsh giants lavish attention on favored pets: krooths, giant octopuses, or primeval creatures like dinosaurs and the crocodilian deinosuchuses.</p>\n<p>Barely topping 11 feet tall and 1,000 pounds, marsh giants are small for giants but make up for their stature with their zealotry.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Giants are massive humanoid creatures who live in remote regions throughout the world. They vary widely but are united in their hunger, requiring sustenance of their own element along with the feasts one would expect from such a massive humanoid. Although a simple matter for some giants, more esoteric types find this need a harsh reality. While a massive fistful of ice or snow alongside their meal will satisfy a frost giant, shadow giants hunger for the coagulated shadows of the Netherworld.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Drowning Hook","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["primal","water"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> A creature is Prone within the marsh giant's reach</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The marsh giant uses its gaff to push the creature down as water bubbles up below it. The target becomes submerged in water until they are no longer prone and must hold their breath if they cannot breathe water. They take 2d10 bludgeoning damage (DC 21 basic Fortitude save) and lose 3 rounds worth of air if they fail the save.</p>"},{"n":"Twist the Hook","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The marsh giant makes a melee Strike with its gaff. If it hits, it twists and yanks the gaff to knock the target Prone and create an awful wound, dealing 2d4 persistent bleed damage to the creature.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-08/lyari-zinfeld":{"lang":["Common","Chthonian","Draconic","Elven","Fey","Necril","Shadowtongue"],"lore":[["Elven Lore",14],["Library Lore",16]],"gear":["Duty's Soulshackle","Books","Writing Set"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Consume Flesh","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> Lyari is adjacent to the corpse of a creature that died within the last hour</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Lyari devours a chunk of the corpse and regains 1d6 healing Hit Points. She can regain Hit Points from any given corpse only once.</p>"},{"n":"Nihilistic Truthsayer","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>Lyari's solitary time in the depths and unique perspective on existence makes her shockingly accepting of terrible universal truths that others don't want to hear. She calmly lays into an enemy within 30 feet, reminding them of existential frailty, presumed insecurities, and inevitable failures in a logical and level manner. The target must attempt a DC 16 Will save. On a failure, they are Frightened 2 (Frightened 3 and Fleeing for 1 round on a critical failure). Regardless of the result of its save, the target is temporarily immune for 1 hour.</p>"},{"n":"Swift Leap","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["move"],"f":"","d":"<p>Lyari jumps up to half her Speed. This movement doesn't trigger reactions.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-08/lyari-zinfeld-3-4":{"lang":["Common","Chthonian","Draconic","Elven","Fey","Necril","Shadowtongue"],"lore":[["Elven Lore",17],["Library Lore",20]],"gear":["Duty's Soulshackle","Books","Writing Set"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Consume Flesh","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> Lyari is adjacent to the corpse of a creature that died within the last hour</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Lyari devours a chunk of the corpse and regains 1d6 healing Hit Points. She can regain Hit Points from any given corpse only once.</p>"},{"n":"Nihilistic Truthsayer","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>Lyari's solitary time in the depths and unique perspective on existence makes her shockingly accepting of terrible universal truths that others don't want to hear. She calmly lays into an enemy within 30 feet, reminding them of existential frailty, presumed insecurities, and inevitable failures in a logical and level manner. The target must attempt a DC 19 Will save. On a failure, they are Frightened 2 (Frightened 3 and Fleeing for 1 round on a critical failure). Regardless of the result of its save, the target is temporarily immune for 1 hour.</p>"},{"n":"Swift Leap","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["move"],"f":"","d":"<p>Lyari jumps up to half her Speed. This movement doesn't trigger reactions.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-22/marcoss-marauders":{"lang":["Common"],"lore":[["Warfare Lore",21]],"notes":{"speed":"troop movement"},"abilities":[{"n":"Troop Defenses","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Troops are composed of many individuals, represented by four \"segments\" on a battle grid. Each segment is 10 feet on each side and as tall as the individual members of the troop. Segments must remain contiguous. Each one has to share at least 5 feet of one of its edges with another segment—being adjacent on a diagonal isn't sufficient! You can measure flanking, cover, and the like using the center of any segment.</p>\n<p>A troop has two Hit Point thresholds in its HP entry and loses segments as it crosses thresholds. Typically, the higher threshold is at 2/3 of the troop's maximum Hit Points and the lower is at 1/3 of its maximum. Once the troop drops below the higher threshold, it loses one segment, leaving three segments (12 squares) remaining and setting the first threshold as the troop's new maximum Hit Points. This repeats when the troop drops below the lower threshold, leaving two segments (8 squares). At 0 Hit Points, the troop disperses entirely, with the few remaining members surrendering, Fleeing, or easily dispatched, as determined by the GM. Typically the creature who caused the troop to lose a segment decides which to remove, or the GM decides when a specific creature wasn't responsible. To restore lost segments and maximum Hit Points, a troop needs to spend downtime to use long-term treatment on casualties or recruit new members to replace the fallen.</p>\n<p>Troops are typically immune to non-damaging effects that target a single creature, such as a Charm spell or the Demoralize action. An ability that can target 5 or more creatures can target an entire segment, increasing to two segments if it can target 10 or more creatures and to the entire troop if it can target 20 or more creatures. An ability that affects all creatures in a certain range affects all segments in range (make any checks or saves separately for each segment). As examples, an 8th rank <em>charm</em> spell (with 10 targets) can affect two segments, and an ability that Demoralizes all creatures within 30 feet of you would affect all segments that are fully within that range. A non-damaging ability that would prevent a segment from acting, cause them to flee, or otherwise make them unable to function as part of the troop for a round or more removes the segment entirely. The troop loses a number of HP required to bring it to the next threshold. If an ability both deals damage and has a non-damaging effect, apply the damage then the rest of the effect.</p></p>"},{"n":"Troop Movement","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Whenever a troop moves, you move one of its segments and the other segments follow behind it. At the end of the movement, you can group the other segments adjacent to the one you moved as you see fit, provided none of them moves farther than the moving segment. If you choose not to move the troop any distance, you can instead reshape the position of all the segments as long as one stays in place.</p></p>"},{"n":"Prepared for Hell","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The Marauders have come prepared to fight devils and the damage from Short Salvo and Slashing Blades is silver. The damage from Punitive Attack is also silver, if the troop possesses that ability.</p>"},{"n":"Short Salvo","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The Marauders draw and fire a barrage of arrows from their shortbows. The salvo is a 10-foot burst within 60 feet that deals 4d8 piercing damage (DC 27 basic Reflex save). When the Marauders are reduced to 2 segments, this area decreases to a 5-foot burst.</p>"},{"n":"Slashing Blades","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The Marauders attack each enemy in a 5-foot emanation with their swords, with a DC 27 basic Reflex save. The damage depends on the number of actions.</p>\n<p>1 2d6+3 slashing damage</p>\n<p>2 4d6+7 slashing damage</p>\n<p>3 5d6+10 slashing damage</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-07/marshy-snapdrake":{"lang":["Arboreal","Common","Muan","can't speak any language"],"notes":{"speed":"greater forest passage"},"flavor":"<p>Skilled kizidhar mages and gardeners handcraft these lovely creatures as much for their shuyookhs' aesthetic pleasure as for their protection. Creating a snapdrake requires first painstakingly constructing a frame of living wood in the shape of a drake before weaving thousands of colorful snapdragon flowers into intricate patterns to form its body and scales. Once complete, snapdrakes often serve kizidhars as a combination of guards, pets, and decorations for as long as they are well fed.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Alluring Scent","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","olfactory","plant","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet. A creature that enters the emanation must attempt a DC 25 Will save. On a failure, the target is Fascinated by the snapdrake and must use at least 1 action on its next turn to Stride closer to the snapdrake. On a success, the target is immune to the snapdrake's alluring scent for 1 hour.</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike (Tail Scythe Only)","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Greater Marsh Passage","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The marshy snapdrake ignores difficult terrain and greater difficult terrain from marshy ground and fungi</p>"},{"n":"Marshy Snapdrake Pollen","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["plant","poison"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 25 Fortitude;</p>\n<p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 8 rounds</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 1</strong> 1d6 poison damage plus Dazzled 1 (1 round)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 2</strong> 1d6 poison damage plus dazzled 1 and Sickened 1 (2 rounds)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 3</strong> 2d6 poison damage plus Confused and sickened 1 (2 rounds)</p>"},{"n":"Speed Surge","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["move"],"f":"3 times per day","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> 3 times per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The marshy snapdrake Strides or Flies up to twice its Speed</p>"},{"n":"Spray Pollen","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","plant","poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>The marshy snapdrake breathes a blast of pollen in a 40-foot cone Creatures caught in the blast must succeed at a DC 25 Reflex save or be exposed to marshy snapdrake pollen The marshy snapdrake can't use Spray Pollen again for 1d6 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-04/murderous-crowd":{"description":"<p>Concerned citizens shout slogans about the dangers of dealing with Cheliax and throw bricks at Chelaxian sympathizers.</p>","disable":"<p>Succeed at two of the following checks in any combination: DC 27 Athletics (trained) to confiscate dangerous debris, DC 27 Diplomacy (trained) to calm the crowd, DC 25 Intimidation (untrained) to scare the crowd away, DC 30 Will (trained) to maintain a brave and confident demeanor; an effect such as Calm that can target an area counts as one automatic success.</p>","routine":"<p>(three actions) The unruly crowd uses an action to chant a Catchy Slogan if it is not already benefiting from the effect It uses Shake Confidence once per turn and uses its remaining actions for cobblestone Strikes.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained) Characters automatically detect this hazard when they open the door to the Grand Hall.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"There They Are!","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature opens the door to the Grand Hall</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The unruly crowd rolls Initiative.</p>"},{"n":"Catchy Slogan","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","emotion","linguistic"],"f":"","d":"<p>All the hazards in a 30-foot emanation gain a +1 status bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls for 1 round.</p>\n<p>Effect: Catchy Slogan</p>"},{"n":"Shake Confidence","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","emotion"],"f":"","d":"<p>The unruly crowd targets a creature within 30 feet The creature must attempt a DC 27 Will save</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected and immune to Shake Confidence for 24 hours</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature becomes Frightened 1</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature becomes Frightened 2</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature becomes frightened 2 and Stupefied 1.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-03/naiad-commander":{"lang":["Common","Elven","Fey","Thalassic"],"lore":[["Sailing Lore",17]],"gear":["Coral Armor"],"flavor":"<p>The captain is the ultimate authority on a vessel, responsible for the livelihood and well-being of everyone on the ship.</p><hr><p>Adventurers may need passage on a swift vessel, or they might face danger from raiders at sea or in coastal settlements.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Animal Empathy","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The naiad can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with animals</p>"},{"n":"Bravery","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the naiad commander rolls a success on a Will save against a fear effect, they get a critical success instead In addition, anytime they gain the Frightened condition, reduce its value by 1.</p>"},{"n":"Dual Disarm","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The naiad commander makes two Strikes, one with their rapier and one with their main-gauche (in either order) If both Strikes hit, the naiad commander can attempt to Disarm the target Their multiple attack penalty increases only after all the attacks are made.</p>"},{"n":"No Quarter!","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","concentrate","emotion","linguistic","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The naiad commander orders their allies to fight without mercy All allied creatures of equal or lower level within 20 feet of the commander gain a +1 status bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls until the end of the naiad commander's next turn.</p>\n<p>Effect: No Quarter!</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-03/naiad-raider":{"lang":["Common","Elven","Fey","Thalassic"],"gear":["Coral Armor"],"flavor":"<p>Criminal organizations are always happy to loan out money at exorbitant rates, and their legbreakers are always happy to collect.</p><hr><p>In the underbelly of society, the lawless reign supreme.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Animal Empathy","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The naiad can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with animals.</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Break Legs!","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The naiad raider makes a maul Strike against an adjacent creature If it hits, the creature is knocked Prone and becomes Clumsy 1 for 1 minute As long as this clumsy condition lasts, the creature also takes a –5-foot penalty to its Speeds and has weakness 5 to the naiad raider's Strikes.</p>\n<p>Effect: Break Legs!</p>"},{"n":"Rushing Strike","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The naiad raider Strides twice If they end their movement within melee reach of an enemy, they can make a melee Strike against that enemy.</p>"},{"n":"Stampeding Shove","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The naiad raider Shoves a creature, gaining a +2 circumstance bonus to their Athletics check if the target is Prone. If the Shove succeeds, the target takes 2d10 bludgeoning damage (double damage on a critical success).</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-03/naiad-ship-hunter":{"lang":["Common","Elven","Fey","Thalassic"],"gear":["Coral Armor"],"flavor":"<p>Bounty hunters are constantly on the move, whether within city walls or the wilderness, trailing their fugitive quarries for capture... or disposal. Often relying on stealth or deception as much as martial skill, bounty hunters employ a vast array of talents to accomplish their goals and collect the hefty payout.</p><hr><p>Whether they're hired to wage war, protect a caravan, or infiltrate an impenetrable fortress, there's ample work for mercenaries all over Golarion.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Animal Empathy","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The naiad can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with animals.</p>"},{"n":"Hunt Prey","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate"],"f":"","d":"<p>The naiad ship hunter designates a single creature they can see and hear, or one they're Tracking or Gathering Information about, as their prey. The naiad ship hunter gains a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to Seek the prey, to Survival checks to Track the prey, and to Diplomacy checks to Gather Information about the prey. This effect lasts until they use Hunt Prey again.</p>"},{"n":"Posse's Edge","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The naiad ship hunter and their allies gain a +1 circumstance bonus on initiative rolls if the opposing side includes their hunted prey.</p>\n<p>Effect: Posse's Edge</p>"},{"n":"Precision Edge","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The frst time the naiad ship hunter hits their hunted prey in a round, they deal an additional 1d8 precision damage.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-03/naiad-warrior":{"lang":["Common","Thalassic"],"lore":[["Ocean Lore",11]],"gear":["Coral Armor"],"abilities":[{"n":"Animal Empathy","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Animal Empathy The naiad can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with animals.</p>"},{"n":"Underwater Awareness","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An enemy Strikes the naiad warrior while they're underwater</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The naiad senses the movement of their enemy in the water and jerks back in time They gain a +2 circumstance bonus to their AC against the triggering attack.</p>"},{"n":"Dive","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The naiad warrior moves up to twice their swim Speed downward.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-03/naiad-water-defender":{"lang":["Common","Elven","Fey","Thalassic"],"lore":[["Underworld Lore",15]],"gear":["Coral Armor"],"flavor":"<p>Gang leaders direct cutthroats, killers, thieves, and toughs. The gang leader often appears alongside a bandit gang or other criminals.</p><hr><p>Villains pursue selfish and cruel goals, trampling over anyone in their way.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Animal Empathy","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The naiad can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with animals</p>"},{"n":"Deny Advantage","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The naiad water defender isn't Off-Guard to creatures of 7th level or lower that are Hidden, Undetected, flanking, or using Surprise Attack.</p>"},{"n":"Evasive Reflexes","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the naiad water defender rolls a success on a Reflex save, they get a critical success instead.</p>"},{"n":"Nimble Dodge","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The naiad water defender is targeted with an attack by an attacker they can see</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The naiad water defender gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against the triggering attack.</p>"},{"n":"Surprise Attacker","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>On the first round of combat, creatures that haven't acted are Off-Guard to the naiad water defender.</p>"},{"n":"Brutal Rally","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","emotion","linguistic","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The naiad water defender rolls a critical hit against a creature</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> All allies that can see the naiad water defender gain a +1 circumstance bonus to attack rolls until the start of the naiad water defender's next turn.</p>\n<p>Effect: Brutal Rally</p>"},{"n":"Gang Up","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Any enemy is Off-Guard against the naiad water defender's melee attacks due to flanking as long as the enemy is within melee reach of both the naiad water defender and one of the naiad water defender's allies.</p>"},{"n":"Quick Draw","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The naiad water defender Interacts to draw a weapon, then Strikes with that weapon</p>"},{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The naiad water defender deals an extra 2d6 precision damage to Off-Guard creatures.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-03/naiad-water-guardian":{"lang":["Common","Elven","Fey","Thalassic"],"gear":["Coral Armor"],"flavor":"<p>Believing the ends justify the means, the unsanctioned sheriff is unafraid to use others for their own gain, through bribes, manipulation, or force.</p><hr><p>These lone wolves have an aura of mystery, bravado, and swagger.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Animal Empathy","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The naiad can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with animals.</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"At My Command","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","concentrate","linguistic","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The naiad water guardian's last action this turn was a successful Strike against a creature within 30 feet</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The naiad yells a command at the creature they hit The target must succeed at a DC 22 Will save or spend the first action on its next turn doing as commanded (or all its actions on its next turn on a critical failure) The naiad can command a creature to approach them, release what its holding, or drop Prone Regardless of the result of its save, the creature is temporarily immune for 10 minutes.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-07/ogre-hunter":{"lang":["Common","Jotun"],"gear":["Ogre Hook","Trident (6)","Breastplate"],"abilities":[{"n":"Always Ready for a Scufe","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature gets in melee range of the ogre hunter</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The ogre hunter draws a melee weapon.</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Hunting Throw","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The ogre hunter makes a ranged strike with their trident within 60 feet without ranged penalties. If the strike hits, it has enough force to knock the target Prone. If the strike was a critical success, the target is also Immobilized by the trident.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-01/olinda-posandi":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic"],"gear":["Dagger","Silver Religious Symbol of Asmodeus"],"abilities":[{"n":"Sacrifice Minion","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["misfortune"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An enemy creature within 15 feet rolls a saving throw</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Destroy one imp minion within 15 feet. The enemy rolls twice and takes the lower result on the saving throw.</p>"},{"n":"Conjure Imp","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per turn","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per turn</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Olinda conjures an imp minion within 20 feet, which can make a melee strike against an adjacent enemy.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-01/olinda-posandi-3-4":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic"],"gear":["Dagger","Silver Religious Symbol of Asmodeus"],"abilities":[{"n":"Sacrifice Minion","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["misfortune"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An enemy creature within 15 feet rolls a saving throw</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Destroy one imp minion within 15 feet. The enemy rolls twice and takes the lower result on the saving throw.</p>"},{"n":"Conjure Imp","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per turn","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per turn</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Olinda conjures an imp minion within 20 feet, which can make a melee strike against an adjacent enemy.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-08/partially-decomposed-rat-swarm":{"notes":{"hp":"negative healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Slow","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A partially decomposed rat swarm is permanently Slowed 1 and can't use reactions.</p>"},{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Swarming Bites","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Each enemy in the swarm's space takes 1d6 piercing damage and must attempt a DC 17 basic Reflex save. A creature that fails its save is exposed to zombie plague.</p>"},{"n":"Zombie Plague","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["disease","divine","void"],"f":"","d":"<p>The sickened and Unconscious conditions from zombie plague can't end or be reduced until the disease is cured.</p>\n<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 14 Fortitude</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 1</strong> carrier with no ill effect (1d4 hours),</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 2</strong> Sickened 1 (1 day),</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 3</strong> sickened 1 and Slowed 1 (1 day),</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 4</strong> unconscious (1 day),</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 5</strong> dead</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-01/pile-of-orts":{"description":"<p>A rift to Hell crackles with unstable energy from the broken summoning circle as a squirming mass of fiends struggles to emerge A blood mist projection of a Hellknight angrily commands them.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 16 Arcana, DC 16 Nature, DC 16 Occultism, or DC 16 Religion (2 actions) (trained) while within 15 feet to weaken the rift, dealing 2d4 spirit damage to it. This damage has the holy trait.</p>","routine":"<p>(1 action) The Hellknight commands the orts, and the trap lashes out at each enemy creature in its space and adjacent, dealing 1d6+3 slashing damage (DC 15 basic Reflex save) If no enemy is in reach, an ort emerges in an adjacent square.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Hellfire","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["aura"],"f":"","d":"<p>All orts within 30 feet have +1 status bonus to hit and deal 1d4 extra fire damage on a hit.</p>"},{"n":"Bubble","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The trap receives a critical hit or critically fails a saving throw</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> One ort emerges adjacent.</p>"},{"n":"Planar Breach","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The magic circle is broken</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The pile disgorges orts and then rolls initiative</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-02/pirate-goblin":{"lang":["Common","Goblin"],"gear":["Dogslicer","Shortbow","Leather Armor","Arrows (10)"],"flavor":"<p>The frontline fighters of goblin tribes prefer to fight in large groups—especially when they can outnumber their foes at least three to one.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>These small humanoids typically have green or gray skin and large heads with wide ears. While some goblins are civilized and have worked hard to be considered upstanding members of humanoid communities, many are impetuous and vicious creatures who delight in wreaking havoc. These goblins think nothing of slaughtering livestock, stealing, or burning down a building purely for momentary delight. They revel in playing malicious tricks on taller humanoids, whom they call \"longshanks.\"</p>\n<p>Goblins are superstitious, with an intense awe of magic and a fascination with fire; goblins who master magic or fire earn great respect from their kin. Most other humanoids find it difficult to understand goblins' outlook: they hate canines but eagerly share their lairs with so-called \"goblin dogs,\" they fearlessly attack larger creatures but are terrified of horses, and they despise vegetables yet consider pickles a delicacy. To a goblin, of course, these are all perfectly sensible life choices.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Tailed Goblin","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A pirate goblin is not Off-Guard while Climbing, can Climb with one hand occupied, and can Trip opponents even if both hands are occupied.</p>"},{"n":"Goblin Scuttle","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An ally ends a move action adjacent to the pirate goblin</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The pirate goblin Steps.</p>"},{"n":"Boarding Action","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The pirate goblin swings on a rope or Strides, moving up to double their Speed. If the pirate boarded or disembarked a boat during this movement, they can make a melee Strike at the end of their movement that deals one extra damage die on a hit.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-02/pirate-gorilla":{"flavor":"<p>Gorillas can be territorial creatures, particularly if provoked by hunters or the presence of more dangerous monsters. A gorilla uses its fangs and powerful arms to bite and pummel trespassers with wild abandon.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>While many apes exhibit peaceful or reclusive behavior, gorillas can be territorial, and the megaprimatus is especially aggressive and dangerous.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Boarding Action","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The pirate gorilla swings on a rope or Strides, moving up to double their Speed. If the pirate boarded or disembarked a boat during this movement, they can make a melee Strike at the end of their movement that deals one extra damage die on a hit.</p>"},{"n":"Frightening Display","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The gorilla beats its chest in a terrifying display. Creatures within 30 feet must attempt a DC 18 Will save. While a creature is frightened by this ability, it is Off-Guard to the gorilla.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> No effect and temporarily immune for 1 minute.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 2.</p>"},{"n":"Well-Trained","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The pirate gorilla is used to taking orders on board the ship. It loses its immunity to linguistic efects, including appeals to surrender.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-08/recently-slain-rat-swarm":{"notes":{"hp":"negative healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Slow","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A partially decomposed rat swarm is permanently Slowed 1 and can't use reactions.</p>"},{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Frenzied Bites","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Each enemy in the swarm's space takes 2d6 piercing damage and must attempt a DC 20 basic Reflex save. A creature that fails its save is exposed to zombie plague.</p>"},{"n":"Zombie Plague","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["disease","divine","void"],"f":"","d":"<p>The sickened and Unconscious conditions from zombie plague can't end or be reduced until the disease is cured.</p>\n<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 17 Fortitude</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 1</strong> carrier with no ill effect (1d4 hours),</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 2</strong> Sickened 1 (1 day),</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 3</strong> sickened 1 and Slowed 1 (1 day),</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 4</strong> unconscious (1 day),</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 5</strong> dead</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-04/rowdy-crowd":{"description":"<p>Concerned citizens shout slogans about the dangers of dealing with Cheliax and throw bricks at Chelaxian sympathizers.</p>","disable":"<p>Succeed at two of the following checks in any combination: DC 22 Athletics (trained) to confiscate dangerous debris, DC 22 Diplomacy (trained) to calm the crowd, DC 20 Intimidation (untrained) to scare the crowd away, DC 24 Will (trained) to maintain a brave and confident demeanor; an effect such as Calm that can target an area counts as one automatic success.</p>","routine":"<p>(three actions) The unruly crowd uses an action to chant a Catchy Slogan if it is not already benefiting from the effect It uses Shake Confidence once per turn and uses its remaining actions for cobblestone Strikes.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained) Characters automatically detect this hazard when they open the door to the Grand Hall.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"There They Are!","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature opens the door to the Grand Hall</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The unruly crowd rolls Initiative.</p>"},{"n":"Catchy Slogan","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","emotion","linguistic"],"f":"","d":"<p>All the hazards in a 30-foot emanation gain a +1 status bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls for 1 round.</p>\n<p>Effect: Catchy Slogan</p>"},{"n":"Shake Confidence","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","emotion"],"f":"","d":"<p>The unruly crowd targets a creature within 30 feet The creature must attempt a DC 22 Will save</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected and immune to Shake Confidence for 24 hours</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature becomes Frightened 1</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature becomes Frightened 2</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature becomes frightened 2 and Stupefied 1.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-08/scaling-the-chain":{"description":"<p>The PCs appear on a gigantic wall of hooked chains dangling in a gray swirling mist. The chains radiate life-chilling energy Cries of innocence and condemnation echo through the mist in Elven. A plane of light 10 feet above eddies and swirls as it dully reflects the PCs below, but the reflections warp and alter the PCs to have sallow complexions like the undead.</p>","disable":"<p>A PC that has ascended to the plane of light (DC 13 Athletics check to Climb; on a critical failure, the PC falls 10 feet before being seized by a chain) can attempt a DC 18 Thievery check to disrupt the plane or a DC 18 Arcana, DC 18 Occultism or DC 18 Religion check to ritually disrupt the haunting. Each success reduces the haunt's actions by one. When the haunt has no more actions, it is disabled and the PCs all return to area <strong>B3</strong>.</p>","reset":"<p>The haunt resets the next time the <em>Soulshackle</em> traps creatures in the library.</p>","routine":"<p>(three actions) The chains rattle and sigh ominously around two different random creatures trapped in the haunt, dealing 1d6+2 void damage (DC 16 basic Will save).</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"The Pain of Devotion","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Hunted by Chains is disabled</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The chains rattle ominously, dealing 1d6+2 void damage to all creatures in the haunt (DC 16 basic Will save). The haunt then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-08/shriveled-leaf-of-talhindir":{"lang":["Necril"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Light Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Attacks against the Leaf of Talhindir are treated as magical if made by a creature who is in magical light or with an object that is in magical light (such as from the Light spell).</p>"},{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Slink in Shadows","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The Leaf of Talhindir can Hide or end its Sneak in a creature's or object's shadow.</p>"},{"n":"Weight of Darkness","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The Leaf of Talhindir made a successful Strike against a living creature with its withered touch on its previous action</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The Leaf of Talhindir chains the soul of the creature. They must attempt a DC 17 Will save. On a failure, the creature is Enfeebled 1. This is cumulative with other enfeebled conditions from other Leaves of Talhindir or shadows, to a maximum of Enfeebled 4. The enfeebled value from Weight of Darkness decreases by 1 every minute.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/quests/skeleton-adept":{"lang":["Common","Jotun"],"lore":[["Scribing Lore",5]],"gear":["Journal","Robes","Writing Set","Scroll Case"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>Adepts have unlocked only the most minor of occult mysteries. A few are chosen by accomplished practitioners for further training.</p><hr><p>Hidden secrets and occult powers have an irresistible lure for many. Since the majority of these NPCs are spellcasters, consider using alternative spell lists to adjust their themes.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Collapse","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The skeleton is critically hit.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The skeleton collapses into a pile of bones and the attack deals only normal damage. The skeleton can reform in a standing position as an action, but until it does, it is Immobilized and Off-Guard.</p>"},{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Focused Thinker","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate"],"f":"","d":"<p>The adept concentrates to muster knowledge and wisdom. While focusing, they gain a +2 status bonus to checks to Recall Knowledge, but take a –2 penalty to Perception. They can Dismiss this focused state.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/quests/skeleton-coven-aspirant":{"lang":["Common","Fey","Jotun"],"gear":["Dagger","Dart (4)","Cauldron"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing","saves":"shared confidence"},"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>Only the foolish would bring themselves to the attention of hags, but some aspirants strive to join a hag coven out of a desire for power or companionship.</p><hr><p>Hidden secrets and occult powers have an irresistible lure for many. Since the majority of these NPCs are spellcasters, consider using alternative spell lists to adjust their themes.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Collapse","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The skeleton is critically hit.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The skeleton collapses into a pile of bones and the attack deals only normal damage. The skeleton can reform in a standing position as an action, but until it does, it is Immobilized and Off-Guard.</p>"},{"n":"Shared Confidence","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a coven aspirant is within 30 feet of at least two allies, they and their allies gain a +1 status bonus to Will saves.</p>\n<p>Effect: Shared Confidence</p>"},{"n":"Forge Pact","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","concentrate","linguistic","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The coven aspirant forms a temporary coven with two or more willing creatures within 30 feet, all of whom must be able to cast spells.</p>\n<p>Members of the temporary coven can cast Charm, Entangling Flora, and Illusory Disguise as 2nd-rank occult innate spells at will, using DC 17 or their spellcasting DC, whichever is higher.</p>\n<p>The coven is dissolved after 3 rounds or when all but one member is dead, whichever comes first. A creature can be a member of only one temporary coven at a time and can join a temporary coven no more than once per 24 hours.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/quests/skeleton-wolfguard":{"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"flavor":"<p>Without the burden of flesh, skeletal wolves charge across the battlefield with terrifying speed.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Among the ranks of the dead, none are so numerous, nor so varied, as the skeleton. While most are almost entirely made from bone, some maintain a few scraps of flesh to aid them in movement, such as wing membranes.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Screaming Skull","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The skeleton removes its skull and throws it, making a jaws attack with a range of 20 feet. It then attempts to Demoralize each foe within 10 feet of the target.</p>\n<p>The head bounces, rolls, or even flies back, returning to the skeleton at the start of its next turn. The skeleton is Blinded until then.</p>"},{"n":"Surge of Speed","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The wolf skeleton Strides three times, but it's Off-Guard until the start of its next turn.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-08/talhindirs-autumn":{"description":"<p>All lights in the room snap on, just as Lyari remembers the day of her death. A susurrus of accusations and a guilty verdict fill the air. Ghostly elven warriors disappear and reappear in a disorienting and implacable advance.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 18 Athletics to stand against the force of the verdict, or DC 18 Arcana, DC 18 Occultism, or DC 18 Religion to ritually disrupt the haunting. Each success reduces the haunt's actions by one When the haunt has no more actions, it is disabled and the Hunted by Chains haunt triggers.</p>","reset":"<p>The haunt resets the next time the <em>Soulshackle</em> traps creatures in the library.</p>","routine":"<p>(two actions) The haunt makes vengeful judgment Strikes against three different random creatures trapped in this haunt. A spectral pool of blood forms beneath any creature knocked Unconscious by this haunt.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained); DC 13 Occultism or DC 13 Religion to notice odd whispers.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Accusations","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["auditory","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The PCs all enter the room</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Accusations of crimes against the crown are whispered throughout the room in Elven. Each living creature in the room must attempt a DC 16 Will save or be Frightened 1. The haunt then rolls initiative.</p>"}],"strikeNotes":{"Vengeful Judgment":"<p>Plus Prone on a critical hit</p>"}},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-08/talhindirs-despair":{"description":"<p>Gentle crying rises to become overwhelming wails. The fungal carvings begin to weep blood that pools around the pillars</p>","disable":"<p>DC 20 Performance (trained) to overpower the frightening cries with a greater sound or DC 18 Occultism or DC 18 Religion (trained) to ritually disrupt the haunting.</p>","reset":"<p>If the haunt is not dispersed, it resets after 1 day.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(expert)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"The Falling Tears","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["auditory","emotion","fear","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature moves within 10 feet of the carving of Viore Ciobanu</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Blood begins to rain from the ceiling. The cries from the statues deal 2d10+13 mental damage to living creatures within the room (DC 20 basic Will save). On a failed save, creatures are also Frightened 1 (or Frightened 2 and Fleeing for 1 minute on a critical failure).</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-08/talhindirs-fall":{"description":"<p>All lights in the room snap on, just as Lyari remembers the day of her death. A susurrus of accusations and a guilty verdict fill the air. Ghostly elven warriors disappear and reappear in a disorienting and implacable advance.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 20 Athletics to stand against the force of the verdict, or DC 20 Arcana, DC 20 Occultism, or DC 20 Religion to ritually disrupt the haunting. Each success reduces the haunt's actions by one When the haunt has no more actions, it is disabled and the Hunted by Chains haunt triggers.</p>","reset":"<p>The haunt resets the next time the <em>Soulshackle</em> traps creatures in the library.</p>","routine":"<p>(two actions) The haunt makes vengeful judgment Strikes against three different random creatures trapped in this haunt. A spectral pool of blood forms beneath any creature knocked Unconscious by this haunt.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained); DC 15 Occultism or DC 15 Religion to notice odd whispers.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Accusations","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["auditory","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The PCs all enter the room</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Accusations of crimes against the crown are whispered throughout the room in Elven. Each living creature in the room must attempt a DC 18 Will save or be Frightened 1. The haunt then rolls initiative.</p>"}],"strikeNotes":{"Vengeful Judgment":"<p>Plus Prone on a critical hit</p>"}},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-08/talhindirs-grief":{"description":"<p>Gentle crying rises to become overwhelming wails. The fungal carvings begin to weep blood that pools around the pillars</p>","disable":"<p>DC 17 Performance (trained) to overpower the frightening cries with a greater sound or DC 15 Occultism or DC 15 Religion (trained) to ritually disrupt the haunting.</p>","reset":"<p>If the haunt is not dispersed, it resets after 1 day.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(expert)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"The Falling Tears","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["auditory","emotion","fear","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature moves within 10 feet of the carving of Viore Ciobanu</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The fungus statues weep blood, and their cries deal 2d6+5 mental damage to living creatures within the room (DC 17 basic Will save). On a failed save, creatures are also Frightened 1 (or Frightened 2 on a critical failure)</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-10/the-scourge-of-woodsedge":{"lang":["Common","Cannot speak"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing","speed":"bladed levitation"},"abilities":[{"n":"Lifesense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The Scourge senses the vital essence of living creatures within range.</p><hr><p><p>Lifesense allows a monster to sense the vital essence of living and undead creatures within the listed range. The sense can distinguish between the vitality energy animating living creatures and the void energy animating undead creatures, much as sight distinguishes colors.</p></p>"},{"n":"Frightful Presence","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>DC 36 Will</p><hr><p><p>A creature that first enters the area must attempt a Will save.</p>\n<p>Regardless of the result of the saving throw, the creature is temporarily immune to this monster's Frightful Presence for 1 minute.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected by the presence.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Frightened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 2.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 4.</p></p><hr><p><em>Note: A radius for this aura was not provided by Paizo</em></p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Bladed Levitation","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The Scourge has a fly speed of 30 feet, but must end its turn within no more than 5 feet off the ground, otherwise it falls and takes damage as normal</p>"},{"n":"Final Execution","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The scourge targets a Paralyzed creature with a blade melee Strike. A successful hit is automatically a critical hit and the target creature must succeed at a DC 36 Fortitude or become Doomed 1. If the target is already doomed, they instead increased their doomed value by 1.</p>"},{"n":"Life Sap","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature damaged by the Scourge's blade Strikes must succeed at a DC 36 Fortitude save or become Drained 1; if the target is already drained, they instead increased their drained value by 1, to a maximum of Drained 3. On a critical failure, the target is also Paralyzed until the end of the Scourge's next turn.</p>"},{"n":"To Shreds","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate","void"],"f":"","d":"<p>The Scourge explodes into a whirling tornado of metal and blades, at the cost of briefly leaving its warshard core vulnerable. All creatures within a 20-foot emanation must succeed at a DC 33 Reflex save or take 10d10 slashing plus 3d8 void damage. The Scourge can't use To Shreds for 1d4 rounds.</p>\n<p>If the Scourge is targeted by a Reactive Strike as a result of using this action, it takes a –2 circumstance penalty to its AC; if the Reactive Strike disrupts this action, this penalty remains until the start of the Scourge's next turn.</p>\n<p>Effect: To Shreds (AC Penalty)</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-05/thoroughbred-nightmare":{"lang":["Chthonian","Daemonic","Diabolic"],"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>Nightmares are flaming equine harbingers of death.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Smoke","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura"],"f":"","d":"<p>15 feet. The nightmare continually exhales black smoke Creatures within the aura are Concealed to those outside it, and creatures outside the aura are concealed to creatures within it. Nightmares and their riders can see through this smoke. A creature that begins its turn in the area must succeed at a DC 25 Fortitude save or be Sickened 2. It's then temporarily immune to being sickened by the smoke for 1 minute. This is an inhaled poison, and the nightmare and its rider are immune to it.</p>"},{"n":"Flaming Gallop","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["divine","fire","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>The nightmare Strides or Flies up to triple its Speed. Its hooves burst with intense flame, dealing 5d6 fire damage with a DC 28 basic Reflex save to each creature other than the nightmare's rider that the nightmare moves adjacent to during its gallop. Each creature can be affected only once during a single use of Flaming Gallop.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-03/timonithaea":{"lang":["Common","Elven","Fey","Thalassic"],"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>Naiad queens rule over pristine wildernesses centered around untouched lakes, massive rivers, or other collective bodies of fresh water. Bards' songs and artists' paintings of these powerful nymphs tend to depict naiad queens in their slightly more humanoid forms, which they don when they make the rare journey into civilized lands to garner allies, gather news, or gauge threats.</p>\n<p>Most naiad queens treat those who respect their domains with kindness, but they're fierce—and quick to eliminate foes. Their blinding beauty and breadth of offensive spells make naiad queens fierce opponents if forced into a fight.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Nymphs are a family of fey that take the form of beautiful humanoids with elven features and have a deep association with the natural world. The most common of their kind are the dryads, which are spirits that embody great trees, but many other kinds of nymphs exist, including naiads, who watch over bodies of water. All nymphs are guardians of some element of nature, typically a specific tree or pond, or even-in the case of nymph queens-whole forests or massive bodies of water</p>\n<h2>Nymph Queens</h2>\n<p>Nymph queens are powerful nymphs who rule over entire regions of untouched wilderness, not just single trees or ponds. Every variety of nymph can have a queen. Naiad queens are among the most prominent, and more often interact with nearby mortals. Thus, some scholars refer to naiad queens as simply \"nymphs.\"</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Animal Empathy","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The naiad can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with animals.</p>"},{"n":"Tied to the Land","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Timonithaea is tied to a body of water or area with a great deal of water features.</p><hr><p>A nymph queen is intrinsically tied to a specific region. As long as the queen is healthy, the environment is exceptionally resilient, allowing the nymph queen to automatically attempt to counteract any spell that would harm the environment (such as the Blight ritual), using her spell DC with a counteract rank equal to the highest-rank druid spell she can cast.</p>\n<p>When the nymph queen becomes physically or psychologically unhealthy, however, her warded region eventually becomes twisted or unhealthy as well. In that case, restoring the nymph queen swiftly heals the entire region.</p>"},{"n":"Timonithaea's Calling","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Timonithaea channels magical energy into the Enoménos crown to telepathically communicate with creatures who are beneath the water within 20 miles of Naós tou Neroú.</p>"},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Nymph's Beauty","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","emotion","mental","primal","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet. DC 23 Will save.</p><hr><p>A creature that fails its save is Stunned 1 and becomes stunned 1 each time it starts its turn within the aura for the next 24 hours, even if it can't see Timonithaea.</p>"},{"n":"Water Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["healing","primal","vitality"],"f":"","d":"<p>For every 10 minutes a naiad spends soaking in any body of water in her domain, she regains 30 Hit Points.</p>"},{"n":"Change Shape","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["polymorph","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>Nymph queens can transform between their original form, which looks much like a typical nymph of their kind, and any Small or Medium humanoid form, typically choosing a more humanoid-looking version of their natural form.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><p>The monster changes its shape indefinitely. It can use this action again to return to its natural shape or adopt a new shape. Unless otherwise noted, a monster cannot use Change Shape to appear as a specific individual. Using Change Shape counts as creating a disguise for the Impersonate use of Deception. The monster's transformation automatically defeats Perception DCs to determine whether the creature is a member of the ancestry or creature type into which it transformed, and it gains a +4 status bonus to its Deception DC to prevent others from seeing through its disguise. Change Shape abilities specify what shapes the monster can adopt. The monster doesn't gain any special abilities of the new shape, only its physical form. For example, in each shape, it replaces its normal Speeds and Strikes, and might potentially change its senses or size. Any changes are listed in its stat block.</p></p>"},{"n":"Focus Beauty","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["emotion","mental","primal","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>If a target already affected by nymph's beauty fails its save, the image of the queen sears into the creature's mind, effectively blinding the creature until its vision is restored with sound body or a similar effect.</p>\n<p>The naiad queen can Dismiss the effect.</p><hr><p>The nymph queen focuses her beauty upon a target, who must attempt a save against her nymph's beauty aura (DC 23 Will save). If the creature fails and was already affected by the aura, it takes a greater effect described in the nymph queen's entry.</p>\n<p>A nymph queen can Focus Beauty on a given creature only once per turn.</p>"},{"n":"Inspiration","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["emotion","mental","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The nymph queen inspires a single intelligent creature by giving that creature a token of her favor, typically a lock of her hair, though it can be some other significant object as well. As long as the creature carries her token and remains in good standing with her, the creature gains a +1 status bonus to all Crafting checks, Performance checks, and Will saves.</p>\n<p>If the nymph grants her token to a bard, and she's the bard's muse, the queen chooses one additional benefit granted by her token: a +1 status bonus to all Lore checks, a +2 status bonus to Performance checks when determining the effects of compositions, a +4 status bonus to untrained skill checks, or a +2 status bonus to Will saves against fey.</p>\n<p>Effect: Nymph Queen's Inspiration</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-03/timonithaea-7-9":{"lang":["Common","Elven","Fey","Thalassic"],"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>Naiad queens rule over pristine wildernesses centered around untouched lakes, massive rivers, or other collective bodies of fresh water. Bards' songs and artists' paintings of these powerful nymphs tend to depict naiad queens in their slightly more humanoid forms, which they don when they make the rare journey into civilized lands to garner allies, gather news, or gauge threats.</p>\n<p>Most naiad queens treat those who respect their domains with kindness, but they're fierce—and quick to eliminate foes. Their blinding beauty and breadth of offensive spells make naiad queens fierce opponents if forced into a fight.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Nymphs are a family of fey that take the form of beautiful humanoids with elven features and have a deep association with the natural world. The most common of their kind are the dryads, which are spirits that embody great trees, but many other kinds of nymphs exist, including naiads, who watch over bodies of water. All nymphs are guardians of some element of nature, typically a specific tree or pond, or even-in the case of nymph queens-whole forests or massive bodies of water</p>\n<h2>Nymph Queens</h2>\n<p>Nymph queens are powerful nymphs who rule over entire regions of untouched wilderness, not just single trees or ponds. Every variety of nymph can have a queen. Naiad queens are among the most prominent, and more often interact with nearby mortals. Thus, some scholars refer to naiad queens as simply \"nymphs.\"</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Animal Empathy","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The naiad can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with animals.</p>"},{"n":"Tied to the Land","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Timonithaea is tied to a body of water or area with a great deal of water features.</p><hr><p>A nymph queen is intrinsically tied to a specific region. As long as the queen is healthy, the environment is exceptionally resilient, allowing the nymph queen to automatically attempt to counteract any spell that would harm the environment (such as the Blight ritual), using her spell DC with a counteract rank equal to the highest-rank druid spell she can cast.</p>\n<p>When the nymph queen becomes physically or psychologically unhealthy, however, her warded region eventually becomes twisted or unhealthy as well. In that case, restoring the nymph queen swiftly heals the entire region.</p>"},{"n":"Timonithaea's Calling","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Timonithaea channels magical energy into the Enoménos crown to telepathically communicate with creatures who are beneath the water within 20 miles of Naós tou Neroú.</p>"},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Nymph's Beauty","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","emotion","mental","primal","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet. DC 26 Will save.</p><hr><p>A creature that fails its save is Stunned 1 and becomes stunned 1 each time it starts its turn within the aura for the next 24 hours, even if it can't see Timonithaea.</p>"},{"n":"Water Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["healing","primal","vitality"],"f":"","d":"<p>For every 10 minutes a naiad spends soaking in any body of water in her domain, she regains 30 Hit Points.</p>"},{"n":"Change Shape","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["polymorph","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>Nymph queens can transform between their original form, which looks much like a typical nymph of their kind, and any Small or Medium humanoid form, typically choosing a more humanoid-looking version of their natural form.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><p>The monster changes its shape indefinitely. It can use this action again to return to its natural shape or adopt a new shape. Unless otherwise noted, a monster cannot use Change Shape to appear as a specific individual. Using Change Shape counts as creating a disguise for the Impersonate use of Deception. The monster's transformation automatically defeats Perception DCs to determine whether the creature is a member of the ancestry or creature type into which it transformed, and it gains a +4 status bonus to its Deception DC to prevent others from seeing through its disguise. Change Shape abilities specify what shapes the monster can adopt. The monster doesn't gain any special abilities of the new shape, only its physical form. For example, in each shape, it replaces its normal Speeds and Strikes, and might potentially change its senses or size. Any changes are listed in its stat block.</p></p>"},{"n":"Focus Beauty","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["emotion","mental","primal","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>If a target already affected by nymph's beauty fails its save, the image of the queen sears into the creature's mind, effectively blinding the creature until its vision is restored with sound body or a similar effect.</p>\n<p>The naiad queen can Dismiss the effect.</p><hr><p>The nymph queen focuses her beauty upon a target, who must attempt a save against her nymph's beauty aura (DC 26 Will save). If the creature fails and was already affected by the aura, it takes a greater effect described in the nymph queen's entry.</p>\n<p>A nymph queen can Focus Beauty on a given creature only once per turn.</p>"},{"n":"Inspiration","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["emotion","mental","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The nymph queen inspires a single intelligent creature by giving that creature a token of her favor, typically a lock of her hair, though it can be some other significant object as well. As long as the creature carries her token and remains in good standing with her, the creature gains a +1 status bonus to all Crafting checks, Performance checks, and Will saves.</p>\n<p>If the nymph grants her token to a bard, and she's the bard's muse, the queen chooses one additional benefit granted by her token: a +1 status bonus to all Lore checks, a +2 status bonus to Performance checks when determining the effects of compositions, a +4 status bonus to untrained skill checks, or a +2 status bonus to Will saves against fey.</p>\n<p>Effect: Nymph Queen's Inspiration</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-10/torn-trio":{"lang":["Common","Necril","can't speak any language"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Bound Limbs","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A torn trio ordinarily has three severed limbs tethered to a central point by near-incorporeal ropes. A limb is essentially cut away from the central point and rendered nonfunctional each time the torn quartet loses 60 Hit Points (so at 120 Hit Points, the torn quartet has two functional limbs, at 60 Hit Points, it has one functional limb). Each functioning limb can Grapple separate creatures within reach, or multiple functioning limbs can Grapple the same creature; for each additional limb used to Grapple a creature, the Escape DC increases by 2.</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike (See Split Reactions)","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Replacement Parts","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A torn trio can spend 1 minute tearing apart the corpse of a humanoid creature that was killed within the last hour to regain 60 Hit Points and restore one of its nonfunctioning limbs. A torn trio can't have more than three limbs.</p>"},{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Flurry of Limbs","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The torn trio makes a number of limb Strikes up to its number of functioning limbs, each against a different target. These attacks count toward the torn trio's multiple attack penalty, but the multiple attack penalty doesn't increase until after the torn trio makes all its attacks.</p>"},{"n":"Split Reactions","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A torn trio has a number of reactions per round equal to its number of still-functioning limbs, which it can use only to make Reactive Strikes. It can't use more than 1 reaction on the same triggering action, even if a creature leaves several squares within its reach, and the torn trio must use a different limb for each Reactive Strike it makes. Whenever one of the torn trio's limbs is rendered nonfunctional, the torn trio loses one of its reactions.</p>"},{"n":"Tear Asunder","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The torn trio has a creature Grabbed or Restrained by at least two limbs</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The creature takes 5d6+2 slashing damage for each limb currently grabbing or restraining it (maximum 15d6), with a DC 30 basic Fortitude save. On a critical failure, the creature also loses a random body part, and one of the torn trio's limbs is now no longer grabbing or restraining it.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-09/undead-hellknight":{"lore":[["Warfare Lore",8]],"gear":["Morningstar","Spear","Steel Shield","Hellknight Plate"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Shield Block","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster has its shield raised and takes damage from a physical attack.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster snaps its shield into place to deflect a blow. The shield prevents the monster from taking an amount of damage up to the shield's Hardness. The monster and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.</p></p>"},{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Damned Restoration","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> An undead target within reach regains 2d6 healing Hit Points and gains a +2 status bonus to damage rolls for 1 round.</p>\n<p>Effect: Damned Restoration</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-12/undead-hellknight-7-12":{"lang":["Common"],"gear":["War Flail","Hellknight Plate"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Drain Vitality","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The undead Hellknight's previous action was a successful Grab.</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The undead Hellknight deals 3d8 void damage to the target and gains temporary Hit Points equal to the damage dealt for 1 hour.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-12/undead-hellknight-armiger":{"lang":["Common"],"gear":["War Flail","Hellknight Plate"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Drain Vitality","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The undead Hellknight's previous action was a successful Grab.</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The undead Hellknight deals 1d8 void damage to the target and gains temporary Hit Points equal to the damage dealt for 1 hour.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-12/undead-hellknight-maralictor":{"lang":["Common"],"gear":["War Flail","Warhammer","Hellknight Plate"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Hammer and Flail","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The undead Hellknight maralictor makes a war flail and a warhammer Strike against the same target. If both Strikes hit, the damage counts as one source for overcoming resistances, Additionally, the target takes an additional 2d6 void damage and the maralictor gains temporary Hit Points equal to this void damage for 1 hour.</p>"},{"n":"Void Energy Burst","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The undead Hellknight maralictor has temporary Hit Points</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Undead energy erupts from the maralictor. All living creatures within a 20-foot emanation take void damage equal to twice the maralictor's temporary Hit Points; the maralictor then loses all temporary Hit Points.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-04/unruly-crowd":{"description":"<p>Concerned citizens shout slogans about the dangers of dealing with Cheliax and throw bricks at Chelaxian sympathizers.</p>","disable":"<p>Succeed at two of the following checks in any combination: DC 20 Athletics (trained) to confiscate dangerous debris, DC 20 Diplomacy (trained) to calm the crowd, DC 18 Intimidation (untrained) to scare the crowd away, DC 22 Will (trained) to maintain a brave and confident demeanor; an effect such as Calm that can target an area counts as one automatic success.</p>","routine":"<p>(three actions) The unruly crowd uses an action to chant a Catchy Slogan if it is not already benefiting from the effect It uses Shake Confidence once per turn and uses its remaining actions for cobblestone Strikes.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained) Characters automatically detect this hazard when they open the door to the Grand Hall.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"There They Are!","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature opens the door to the Grand Hall</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The unruly crowd rolls Initiative.</p>"},{"n":"Catchy Slogan","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","emotion","linguistic"],"f":"","d":"<p>All the hazards in a 30-foot emanation gain a +1 status bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls for 1 round.</p>\n<p>Effect: Catchy Slogan</p>"},{"n":"Shake Confidence","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","emotion"],"f":"","d":"<p>The unruly crowd targets a creature within 30 feet The creature must attempt a DC 20 Will save</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected and immune to Shake Confidence for 24 hours</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature becomes Frightened 1</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature becomes Frightened 2</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature becomes frightened 2 and Stupefied 1.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-04/violent-crowd":{"description":"<p>Concerned citizens shout slogans about the dangers of dealing with Cheliax and throw bricks at Chelaxian sympathizers.</p>","disable":"<p>Succeed at two of the following checks in any combination: DC 25 Athletics (trained) to confiscate dangerous debris, DC 25 Diplomacy (trained) to calm the crowd, DC 23 Intimidation (untrained) to scare the crowd away, DC 28 Will (trained) to maintain a brave and confident demeanor; an effect such as Calm that can target an area counts as one automatic success.</p>","routine":"<p>(three actions) The unruly crowd uses an action to chant a Catchy Slogan if it is not already benefiting from the effect It uses Shake Confidence once per turn and uses its remaining actions for cobblestone Strikes.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained) Characters automatically detect this hazard when they open the door to the Grand Hall.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"There They Are!","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature opens the door to the Grand Hall</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The unruly crowd rolls Initiative.</p>"},{"n":"Catchy Slogan","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","emotion","linguistic"],"f":"","d":"<p>All the hazards in a 30-foot emanation gain a +1 status bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls for 1 round.</p>\n<p>Effect: Catchy Slogan</p>"},{"n":"Shake Confidence","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","emotion"],"f":"","d":"<p>The unruly crowd targets a creature within 30 feet The creature must attempt a DC 25 Will save</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected and immune to Shake Confidence for 24 hours</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature becomes Frightened 1</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature becomes Frightened 2</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature becomes frightened 2 and Stupefied 1.</p>"}]},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-16/warp-pillar":{"description":"<p>A time-disrupting field shimmers around a 9-foot-tall pillar of obsidian and bronze that magically slides across the room.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 18 Arcana, DC 18 Crafting, DC 18 Occultism, or DC 18 Thievery; three successes deactivates a pillar, as does destroying it.</p>","reset":"<p>If the pillar isn't destroyed, it resets 1 minute after making no time drain attacks.</p>","routine":"<p>(two actions) The pillar Steps or Strides to get as close to as many targets as possible, then makes a time drain Strike against each creature within its reach.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained); DC 18 Perception to realize the pillars can move, noticing the pillar has a DC of 0.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Time Shift","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature attacks the pillar or approaches within 5 feet of it, or the other warp pillar activates</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The trap casts Slow (DC 18 Fortitude) on a random creature within 30 feet, then rolls initiative.</p>"},{"n":"Speed 30 feet","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""}],"strikeNotes":{"Time Drain":"<p>plus Slowed 1 for 1 round on a hit (Slowed 2 for 1 round on a critical hit); no multiple attack penalty</p>"}},"pfs-season-7-bestiary/7-08/withered-leaf-of-talhindir":{"lang":["Necril"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Light Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Attacks against the Leaf of Talhindir are treated as magical if made by a creature who is in magical light or with an object that is in magical light (such as from the Light spell).</p>"},{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Slink in Shadows","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The Leaf of Talhindir can Hide or end its Sneak in a creature's or object's shadow.</p>"},{"n":"Weight of Darkness","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The Leaf of Talhindir made a successful Strike against a living creature with its withered touch on its previous action</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The Leaf of Talhindir chains the soul of the creature. They must attempt a DC 15 Will save. On a failure, the creature is Enfeebled 1. This is cumulative with other enfeebled conditions from other Leaves of Talhindir or shadows, to a maximum of Enfeebled 4. The enfeebled value from Weight of Darkness decreases by 1 every minute.</p>"}]}});
